 [{:id "action.batch",
   :label "Batch…",
   :params
   "{commands: [{command, params}] (the action's steps), source?: folder (default) | datasets, folder? (required for folder: the source folder), includeSubdirs?: false, destination?: none (default: leave each file open) | saveAndClose (save over the source and close; for source datasets, save the open document over its own file after each data set, and refuse a document that was never saved, was converted from an older version or was restored by Data Recovery, unless a recorded Save or Save As step writes a file first; a Save or Save As step that overrideSave points into destinationFolder makes each data set's file the document's own) | folder (save or export into destinationFolder and close), destinationFolder? (required when destination is folder; also the folder Override Save/Export write into), datasetFileNaming?: fileNumber | fileDataSetName (default) | dataSetName (used only for source datasets; ignored for folder), overrideOpen?: true (skip document.open / file.open steps: the batch opens each source file), overrideSave?: true (point document.save / file.save / file.saveAs at destinationFolder/{stem}.{ext}), overrideExport?: true (point document.export / document.exportSelection the same way, and give document.exportForScreens / assets.export the folder destinationFolder/{stem}, one for each source file or data set, in which the export names its files as it does outside Batch), stopOnError?: true, label?} play the commands on every readable file in folder (and its subfolders when includeSubdirs; {stem} is the file's name without its extension and without trailing periods and spaces, with `-2`, `-3`… added to a name an earlier file used or whose file or folder has the name of one an earlier file wrote or of another source file or a folder of source files in destinationFolder), or on every data set of the open document. Data set names use the document stem plus a three-digit ordinal, the document stem and an underscore plus the data set name, or the data set name alone. Invalid file name characters become `-` and trailing periods and spaces are dropped; a name already used in the batch or whose output file or folder already exists in a destination folder the batch may read and write gets the next free `-2`, `-3` suffix before the format-derived extension. Caps: 500 files or data sets, 8 folder levels, 256 steps. Batches cannot nest, and a prefs.import step is refused (commands[i], from 0) before any file is opened. A switch (includeSubdirs, overrideOpen, overrideSave, overrideExport, stopOnError) that is not true or false, or a source, folder, destination, destinationFolder, datasetFileNaming or label that is not a string, is an error before any folder is made or file opened; null reads as left out. A step that fails is named in the error by its place in commands, from 1, counting the Open steps the batch skips (action step 3 (`object.align`) failed: …); the batch's own opening of a file, choosing of a data set and destination save, export or close give their errors without a step number. → {processed: [{path|dataset, result|error}…], count, failed, stopped, warning?} (warning: for source datasets, when Save and Close without such a step, or a Save, Save a Copy, Save as Template or export step (document.export, exportSelection, exportForScreens, exportPdf, exportEps, exportDxf, exportForWeb, exportForOffice) that writes a file and is not pointed into destinationFolder, saves every data set over the same file)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "addon.arrange.grid",
   :label "Arrange in Grid",
   :params
   "{layout?: \"grid\" (rows and columns) | \"row\" (one row) | \"column\" (one column), columns?: 1..10000 (grid; default ⌈√count⌉; never more than the count), gapX?: pt −1000000..1000000 (10), gapY?: pt −1000000..1000000 (gapX), centerOnArtboard?: false (true: the grid is centred on the artboard under the selection's centre, else the first; false: it starts at the selection's top-left)} lay the selected objects (the top-level ones) out in their stacking order from the back, left to right and top to bottom, as one undo step. Each cell is as wide as the widest object in its column and as tall as the tallest in its row, each object is centred in its cell, and everything is measured by visual bounds (strokes and effects as drawn) → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrange.rs"}
  {:id "addon.arrange.groupOverlapping",
   :label "Group Overlapping Objects",
   :params
   "{} group the selected objects (the top-level ones, at most 20000) wherever their visual bounds overlap or touch, chains included (when A overlaps B and B overlaps C, all three go in one group), as one undo step. Only objects in the same layer or group are grouped together, objects that overlap nothing stay as they are, and each new group goes where its frontmost member was in the stacking order; the new groups and the objects left alone stay selected → {groups: [id…], grouped (how many objects went into groups)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrange.rs"}
  {:id "addon.arrange.randomizeOpacity",
   :label "Randomize Opacity",
   :params
   "{min?: % 0..100 (30), max?: % 0..100 (100; not less than min), seed?: whole number (0; the same seed, objects and range give the same opacities), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} give each selected object (the top-level ones) its own opacity, picked at random and evenly from min to max, as one undo step (none when no opacity changes); it is the object's opacity, as the Transparency panel sets it. On paths directly in a graph series whose opacity changes, the graph stores the opacity and blend mode of the frontmost of them for its next redraw, and on a series group, the group's own (docs/mcp.md) → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrange.rs"}
  {:id "addon.arrange.replace",
   :label "Replace with Top Object",
   :params
   "{fit?: \"keep\" (the copy keeps its size) | \"bounds\" (scaled to the replaced object's width and height) | \"proportional\" (scaled to fit inside them, in proportion) (\"keep\"), scaleStrokes?: the Scale Strokes & Effects preference, keep?: false (true: the replaced objects stay, under their copies)} put a copy of the topmost selected object centred on each of the other selected objects, in that object's place in the stacking order, as one undo step; sizes and centres are measured as object.setBounds measures them, and the copies are selected → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrange.rs"}
  {:id "addon.arrange.size",
   :label "Set Size of Each",
   :params
   "{width?: pt, height?: pt (at least one; each 0.001..1000000), proportional?: false (with only one of them given, the other follows in proportion; else it stays), reference?: 0..8 (the 9-point grid row by row from the top-left; 4, the centre: the point of each object that stays put), scaleStrokes?: the Scale Strokes & Effects preference} give each selected object (the top-level ones) that width and height, measured as object.setBounds measures them (Use Preview Bounds), as one undo step → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrange.rs"}
  {:id "addon.arrange.sort",
   :label "Sort Objects",
   :params
   "{by?: \"width\" | \"height\" | \"area\" (width × height) | \"x\" (left edge) | \"y\" (top edge) | \"opacity\" (%) | \"stacking\" (stacking order, from the back) (\"area\"), apply?: one of the same (\"stacking\"), order?: \"ascending\" (small to large) | \"descending\" (large to small) | \"random\" (\"ascending\"), distribute?: false (true: the values step evenly from the smallest to the largest; false: the objects trade the values they have), seed?: whole number (0; the order \"random\" picks), scaleStrokes?: the Scale Strokes & Effects preference (width, height and area), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} sort the selected objects (the top-level ones, at most 20000) by the attribute `by` and give them the values of `apply` in that order, as one undo step: the first in order gets the smallest value. Sizes and places are measured and set as object.setBounds measures them (Use Preview Bounds), a width, height or area about each object's centre (an area in proportion); stacking order always trades places, and only among the objects in the same layer or group. With apply \"opacity\", on paths directly in a graph series whose opacity changes, the graph stores the opacity and blend mode of the frontmost of them for its next redraw, and on a series group, the group's own (docs/mcp.md). A run that changes nothing makes no step → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrange.rs"}
  {:id "addon.arrange.swap",
   :label "Swap Objects",
   :params
   "{size?: false (true: each also takes the other's width and height), scaleStrokes?: the Scale Strokes & Effects preference} swap the places (bounds centres) of the two selected objects, measured as object.setBounds measures them (Use Preview Bounds), as one undo step. Off unless exactly two objects are selected",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrange.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.alignInPlace",
   :label "Set Alignment, Keep Position",
   :params
   "{align: \"left\"|\"center\"|\"right\", ids?: [id…] (default: the selection; the type they name is taken locked or hidden too)} align every paragraph of each horizontal point type object so, moving the object so its longest line stays where it is (one line: the text doesn't move), as one undo step → {ids (the objects changed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.breakText",
   :label "Break Text",
   :params
   "{by?: \"lines\"|\"paragraphs\"|\"words\"|\"glyphs\" (lines), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection; the type they name is taken locked or hidden too)} each horizontal point or area type object becomes point type objects, one per line, paragraph, word or glyph, each where its characters were and with their character styles, as one undo step; spaces between pieces go, a paragraph's lines stay lines (a wrapped line ends in a line break), justified lines close up, and a paragraph broken out whole keeps its bullet (not its number; other pieces have no list markers). Type on a path, vertical type, threaded type and area type whose text doesn't fit stay as they are → {ids (the pieces, selected), skipped}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.combineText",
   :label "Combine Point Text",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selection; the type they name is taken locked or hidden too)} merge one-line horizontal point type into as few objects as it can, every glyph staying where it was: pieces turned and sheared alike, as visible and as locked (their groups and layers included), whose baselines line up (within 0.4 em; the difference becomes baseline shift) join left to right, a space goes between pieces at least half a space apart, and tracking on the character before each piece keeps the spacing; each object keeps its character styles, and the leftmost piece of each run its place and paint, as one undo step → {ids (the objects made, selected), combined (pieces merged into them)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.deepUngroup",
   :label "Deep Ungroup…",
   :params
   "{includeClipGroups?: bool (false: clipping groups, and the art inside them, stay as they are; true: they are ungrouped too and their clipping paths become plain paths), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} ungroup every level of the groups among the objects, as one undo step when a group goes; each object keeps the opacity of the groups it was in; from the selection, locked and hidden groups stay whole; named by `ids`, the groups it names and the groups in the groups and layers it names are ungrouped even when locked or hidden (a named layer stays), but not those on a locked artboard, and their objects become hidden or locked when a group was; locked and hidden objects stay locked or hidden and are not selected → {ids (the objects selected: those left, or with no group to take apart the selection as it was), ungrouped (groups)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/cleanup.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.fix",
   :label "Fix All Issues",
   :params
   "{scope?: \"selection\"|\"document\", kinds?: [kind…] (default: all; see addon.cleanup.check)} fix the issues addon.cleanup.check finds, in up to three rounds while a round still finds some (a fix can leave issues for another kind), as one undo step: what is empty, unpainted, invisible, duplicated or off the artboards goes, anchors merge, snap or go, tiny handles retract, paths close and needless groups, compound paths and clipping groups give way to their contents → {scope, total, fixed: {kind: count}}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/cleanup.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.joinText",
   :label "Join Point Text",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selection; the type they name is taken locked or hidden too)} join one-line horizontal point type into one point type object, as one undo step: pieces turned and sheared like the top-left one, and as visible and as locked (their groups and layers included), are read as lines (baselines within 0.4 em of each other), top to bottom, each line's pieces left to right with a space between them; each line becomes a paragraph, left aligned, and keeps the distance between baselines as its leading. The text keeps its character styles; the object takes the top-left piece's place and paint, and the other pieces go → {id (selected), joined (pieces merged into it), lines}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.rejoin",
   :label "Rejoin Path Pieces…",
   :params
   "{gap?: pt 0..6 (0.1), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} weld the open paths under the objects whose ends lie within the gap of each other back into paths: an end joins one other end, the one the path turns least to go on into, pieces may run either way, and a chain whose ends meet closes; each path takes the place and paint of its topmost piece, as one undo step when a path is made; from the selection, locked and hidden paths are left out, and named by `ids`, they are taken, but not those on a locked artboard; only pieces alike in being hidden (by themselves or a group or layer above them) and in being locked join; locked and hidden paths made are not selected → {ids, joined (paths made), removed (pieces merged into them)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/cleanup.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.removeBreaks",
   :label "Remove Breaks",
   :params
   "{kind: \"line\"|\"paragraph\", ids?: [id…] (the type they name is taken locked or hidden too)} remove the forced line breaks (line) or paragraph returns (paragraph) in the characters selected with a Type tool (after Select All in a frame of threaded text, in the text of every frame of the story, locked and hidden frames included), else in all the text of the selected type, as one undo step; a break between two words becomes a space, the frames of a threaded story selected all together being read as one text → {ids, removed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.replaceFonts",
   :label "Replace Missing Fonts…",
   :params
   "{font?: family (default: the default type font, Source Sans 3; any of its names)} set every character of the document's type (the type in its opacity masks and in the art of its symbols and patterns included, hidden or locked type and disabled masks too) whose font family isn't available in `font`, in the style it has closest to the one each had, as one undo step → {runs (style runs changed), font}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.resetTextTransform",
   :label "Reset Text Transform",
   :params
   "{scale?: bool (false: the horizontal scale stays; true: it goes too, the object's and every character's), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection; the type they name is taken locked or hidden too)} take the rotation, shear and reflection off each point type object, its size and the centre of its text staying, as one undo step → {ids (the objects changed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.simplify",
   :label "Simplify Anchors (Keep Shape)…",
   :params
   "{tolerance?: 1..100 (20; higher removes more anchors and lets the outline move further from where it was, up to tolerance × 0.02 pt), protectCorners?: bool (false; anchors where the path turns by more than 30° stay), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} remove the anchors each path under the objects can do without, refitting the handles beside each so the outline keeps its shape, as one undo step when a path changes; open ends stay; from the selection, locked and hidden paths are left out, and named by `ids`, the paths of the objects, groups and layers it names are taken even when locked or hidden, but not those on a locked artboard; a changed path loses its selected anchors and segments → {ids, before, after} anchor counts",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/cleanup.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cleanup.splitText",
   :label "Split Text at Cursor",
   :params
   "{} while a Type tool edits horizontal point or area type: the text before the selected characters, they and the text after become point type objects of their own (at a cursor: before and after it), each where its characters were, as one undo step; spaces at the ends of each piece go, and editing ends with the pieces selected → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/text.rs"}
  {:id "addon.color.applyNearestSwatch",
   :label "Apply Nearest Swatch",
   :params
   "{library?: as addon.color.nearestSwatch (default: \"document\"), fill?: true, stroke?: true, ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} give each solid colour and gradient stop of the selected objects' fills and strokes (their type's and those of the objects inside them; gradient meshes too) the colour of its nearest swatch in the library, as addon.color.nearestSwatch finds it, as one undo step (none when nothing changes): a global or spot swatch's colour links to it. A library's swatches the colours take are added to the document's first, as swatch.library.add adds them (a spot colour stays spot); images and patterns keep their colours. On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the new paint of the topmost visible fill and stroke, and on a graph label the new paint of its characters and rows for every label of its kind, and on a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring its rows for every line of its kind (docs/mcp.md) → {changed: paints changed, swatches: [the document swatches the colours took], added: [swatches added to the document]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/color.rs"}
  {:id "addon.color.fillToStroke",
   :label "Apply Fill to Stroke",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, skipNone?: bool} each target's top stroke takes its own top fill, as it is (a colour in its model, a global or spot colour linked at its tint, a gradient or pattern with its placement, None); a stroke given paint at width 0 gets 1 pt, as Swap Fill and Stroke does. Type: each run's stroke takes its own fill, and while the Type tool has characters selected (no ids), only those. A graph's labels keep the paint when the graph is drawn again, and its axis lines, tick marks and radar rings keep their new rows for every line of their kind. On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the paint and weight of the topmost visible stroke when the command wrote that row (exceptions: docs/mcp.md). skipNone: leave alone a target whose fill is None. A target whose stroke already has that paint is left as it is, and when nothing changes no undo step is recorded. The default stroke takes the default fill the same way → {objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/color.rs"}
  {:id "addon.color.filter",
   :label "Apply as Filter",
   :params
   "{effect: a colour adjustment's effect id (adjust.brightnessContrast, adjust.curves, adjust.hueSaturation, adjust.levels, adjust.shiftToColor, adjust.temperatureTint, addon.color.exposure, addon.color.desaturate, addon.color.duotone or addon.color.invert), params?: {…} (as effect.apply; missing keys take the dialog defaults), fill?: true, stroke?: true, includeImages?: true, includePatterns?: true, ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} recolour the objects and everything inside them as the live effect would draw them, but in their colours, as edit.colors.invert does (fills, strokes, type, gradient meshes, embedded images and pattern tiles), as one undo step (none when nothing changes); their effects stay. Duotone links a colour to its one tone's swatch as the live effect does. On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the new paint of the topmost visible fill and stroke, and on a graph label the new paint of its characters and rows for every label of its kind, and on a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring its rows for every line of its kind (docs/mcp.md) → {changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/color.rs"}
  {:id "addon.color.printFixes",
   :label "Print Ink Fixes",
   :params
   "{scope?: \"selection\" (the selection, or `ids`; by default, the document while nothing is selected) | \"document\" (every layer), inkLimit?: total ink % 1..400 (0 or left out: off), excludePureBlack?: true (black-only and grey colours keep their ink), removeWhiteOverprint?: false (white fills and strokes stop overprinting), overprintBlack?: black % 1..100 (black-only and grey fills and strokes this dark or darker overprint, as edit.colors.overprintBlack; 0 or left out: off), textOnly?: false (Overprint Black on type only), fill?: true, stroke?: true, ids?: [id…]} prepare a CMYK document's inks for print as one undo step: CMYK colours (solid, gradient stops, gradient meshes) with more total ink than inkLimit are scaled down to it (colours of spot swatches and Registration stay), white overprint is removed and black overprint set. Refused in RGB documents (File › Document Color Mode › CMYK Color first). On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores a paint the ink limit changes on the topmost visible fill or stroke, and on a graph label the new paint of its characters and rows for every label of its kind, and on a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring its rows for every line of its kind (docs/mcp.md) → {changed, inkLimited: paints and meshes scaled, whiteOverprintRemoved: objects, blackOverprinted: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/color.rs"}
  {:id "addon.color.select",
   :label "Select by Color Kind",
   :params
   "{kind: \"spotColors\" (objects painted with a spot colour swatch, solid or in a gradient's stops) | \"colorEffects\" (objects carrying a visible colour adjustment effect, on themselves or on a fill or stroke) | \"rgbImages\" | \"cmykImages\" | \"grayImages\" (embedded or linked images whose pixels are RGB, CMYK, or grayscale or 1-bit)} select those objects among the ones Select All reaches, inside groups too; locked and hidden ones are left out → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/color.rs"}
  {:id "addon.color.strokeToFill",
   :label "Apply Stroke to Fill",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, skipNone?: bool} each target's top fill takes its own top stroke's paint, as addon.color.fillToStroke does the other way; the stroke itself is unchanged. The default fill takes the default stroke → {objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/color.rs"}
  {:id "addon.color.swatchLegend",
   :label "Create Swatch Legend",
   :params
   "{names?: [swatch name…] (default: every colour swatch of the document, in panel order), columns?: 1..50 (4), size?: chip side in pt 8..1000 (72), gap?: pt 0..1000 (12), values?: [hex|rgb|cmyk|lab|gray…] (each at most once; default: each swatch's own colour model; spot swatches also say spot), x?, y? (the legend's top-left; default: the first artboard's, inset by `gap`)} draw a legend of colour swatches: one square chip per swatch filled with it (linked to it), labelled inside with the swatch name and the values asked for, in black on light chips and white on dark ones, as one group in one undo step; the group is selected → {id, count} (#4919)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/legend.rs"}
  {:id "addon.contour.set",
   :label "Contour",
   :params
   "{offset: pt (negative insets), corners?: \"sharp\"|\"round\"|\"square\" (default sharp; square cuts each corner off flat), miterLimit?: 1..500 (4; sharp corners only)} make a copy of each selected path or shape directly above it with a live Offset Path effect, or, for a selected object that already has one (a Contour), change that effect: nothing is baked (Expand Appearance bakes it) and the original is kept → {ids, created, updated}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/contour.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cutting.banner",
   :label "Banner Hems and Grommets…",
   :params
   "{hem?: pt 0..100000 (72: from each edge to its hem line; 0: no hem lines), grommets?: bool (true), spacing?: pt more than 0 and at most 100000 (1728: the most the grommets on a side are apart), grommetInset?: pt 0..100000 (36: from each edge to the grommets' centers), diameter?: pt 0.01..1000 (27: each grommet mark's circle), top?, right?, bottom?, left?: bool (true: the sides that get a hem and grommets), weight?: pt 0.01..1000 (0.3), swatch?: a color swatch the marks are stroked in (\"[Registration]\"), allArtboards?: bool (default: true when nothing is selected)} mark the hems and grommets of a banner, the selected art's bounds or each artboard: a hem line `hem` inside each chosen edge, running the edge's whole length, and grommet marks (a circle with a cross at its center) `grommetInset` inside each chosen edge, one at each end of the side and the rest spread evenly between them, as few as keep them at most `spacing` apart. One group named Banner Marks per banner, stroked with no fill, on top of the current layer, selected, as one undo step → {id: the first group, ids, hems (hem lines), grommets (grommet marks)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/banner.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cutting.bridges",
   :label "Stencil Bridges…",
   :params
   "{width?: pt 0.01..1000 (2), count?: whole number 1..16 of bridges each island gets (1; fewer where it has no room and more where other islands are joined to the sheet through it), direction?: \"vertical\" | \"horizontal\" | \"shortest\" (the shortest crossing among 12 directions 15° apart) (\"vertical\"), keepOriginal?: true (the selected objects that make up the art go to a new hidden layer named \"Stencil Original\"; false: they are replaced)} cut bridges out of the selected art so that a stencil cut from it holds together: every island (an area the art encloses, such as the inside of an O or a hole in a shape) is joined to the area around the art by strips `width` wide across the art, the shortest crossings first, then spread around the island. The art is measured by the area its outlines enclose, whatever their paint (open paths closed as a fill closes them; type by its glyph outlines; groups by their members; hidden objects left out) and becomes one compound path with the gaps cut, painted as the topmost selected shape, in the place of the topmost selected object that has outlines. Selected objects with no outlines in the art stay where they are. Art with no islands, or none a bridge of the width fits, is left as it is, with a warning and no undo step; islands the cut result still encloses are counted in `unbridged`, with a warning. Art that reaches more than 10000000 pt from the origin, has more than 200000 anchors, whose combined area has more than 4000 outlines, whose outlines need more than 200000 straight segments, or that takes more work to measure than a fixed budget allows is refused. One undo step; the new path is selected → {id, islands, bridges, unbridged, original (the hidden layer's id, or null), warning?}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stencil.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cutting.nest",
   :label "Nest Shapes…",
   :params
   "{roll?: bool (false: a sheet `width` × `height`; true: a roll `width` wide with no end), width?: pt 0..1000000 (0: the artboard's width), height?: pt 0..1000000 (0: the artboard's height; not used with roll), margin?: pt 0..100000 (18: kept clear inside each edge of the sheet; on a roll, the sides and the start), spacing?: pt 0..100000 (9: kept between two objects), rotate?: bool (false: objects keep their orientation; true: an object may turn 90° clockwise where that puts its bottom edge higher, or where only the turned object fits), usePreviewBounds?: bool (true: objects are measured with their strokes and effects, the reach of shadows, glows and blurs included; false: by their geometry), artboard?: index (0-based; the sheet's artboard; default: the artboard under the center of the selection, else the first), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes move with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles)} move the selected objects onto the sheet or roll, which starts at the artboard's top-left corner, packed by their bounding boxes: the tallest first (with rotate, the longest side first), each where its bottom edge is highest and then furthest left, without resizing them. An object on the pixel grid moves by whole points and takes 1 pt more room across and down; a path of a pixel-aligned compound path is not turned. Objects that do not fit on the sheet go in a column to the right of it, `spacing` from its edge and from each other, from its top, in stacking order (back to front). Objects without bounds (an empty group) are not moved. One undo step; nothing changes when no object moves → {placed: count, unplaced: [ids of the objects put beside the sheet], rotated: [ids], skipped: [ids of the objects without bounds], length: pt (from the sheet's top edge to the bottom margin below the lowest object placed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/nest.rs"}
  {:id "addon.cutting.weed",
   :label "Weed Box and Lines…",
   :params
   "{margin?: pt 0..100000 (9: from the art to the weed box), box?: true (false: the weeding lines only), direction?: \"horizontal\" | \"vertical\" | \"both\" (\"both\"), count?: whole number 0..1000 of lines each way (1), spacing?: pt more than 0 and at most 100000 (instead of count, never with it: as few lines as keep them at most this far apart, up to 1000 each way), gap?: pt 0..100000 (0: the lines stop at the art's outlines), weight?: pt 0.01..1000 (0.3), swatch?: a color swatch the lines are stroked in (\"[Registration]\")} add a weed box around the selected art and weeding lines across it that divide it evenly, each running from one side of the box to the other and left out over the art and within `gap` of its outlines, so the waste lifts off in pieces. The art is measured by the outlines a cutter cuts: closed paths enclose their area by their fill rule and open paths are lines, compound paths by all their subpaths, type by its glyph outlines, a clip group by what shows inside its clipping path, images by their frames, placed files by the art they show (by their boxes when the file can't be read), symbol instances by their art and live objects by the art they draw; strokes, effects and hidden objects are left out. One group named Weeding, stroked with no fill, on top of the current layer (outside the clip groups around a group edited in isolation), selected, as one undo step → {id: the group, box: its weed box or null, lines (pieces of weeding line)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/weed.rs"}
  {:id "addon.document.batchTraceFolder",
   :label "Batch Trace Folder",
   :params
   "{folder, destinationFolder, preset?: name (imageTrace.presets; default: Default), expand?: false (true: trace and expand, as Make and Expand), format?: vectorcraft (default)|svg|pdf|ai|eps, includeSubdirs?: false} open each image in folder (png, jpg, tif, bmp, gif, webp, psd), select it, trace it with the preset, save it into destinationFolder as <name>.<ext> (-2, -3… added when that name is taken, so no file is replaced) and close it again, whether it traced or not; the document that was active stays active. Optional settings use their defaults only when omitted; null and values of the wrong type return an error before any image is opened. Caps: 500 images, 8 folder levels; a folder with more than 1,000 entries is refused. Not on the web (no file system) → {traced: [{path, output}], failed: [{path, error}], format} (#4921)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/document.rs"}
  {:id "addon.document.exportAllOpen",
   :label "Export All Open Documents",
   :params
   "{folder, format?: vectorcraft|pdf|svg|svgz|ai|eps (default: pdf)} write a copy of every open document, in tab order, to `folder` as File › Save a Copy writes it, each named after its document (<name>.<ext>; -2, -3… added when that name is taken, so no file is replaced), one self-contained file each with all of its art (images embedded or included, every artboard; no remembered save options apply): every document keeps its path, title and modified state, and no undo step is made. A document that can't be written is listed in `failed` and the others are still written; the active document stays active → {files: [{title, path, warnings}], failed: [{title, error}], format}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/document.rs"}
  {:id "addon.document.saveTimestampedCopy",
   :label "Save a Timestamped Copy",
   :params
   "{folder? (default: the document's own folder; needed for a document never saved), format?: vectorcraft|pdf|svg|svgz|ai|eps (default: the document's own, else vectorcraft), time?: Unix seconds (default: now)} write a copy of the document named <name>_YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM.<ext> (the date and time in UTC; -2, -3… added when that name is taken) as File › Save a Copy writes it: the document keeps its path, title and modified state, and no undo step is made. Off where there is no clock (the web) → {path, format, bytes, warnings}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/document.rs"}
  {:id "addon.document.symbolsFromLayers",
   :label "New Symbols from Layers",
   :params
   "{layers?: [layer id…] (top-level layers; default: those highlighted in the Layers panel when two or more are, else every one), replace?: bool (false: the art stays; true: each layer's art is replaced by an instance of its symbol in the same place)} make one symbol of each layer's art as symbol.new makes one (registration in the centre), named after the layer (with a number added when a symbol has that name), as one undo step. Layers with no art are skipped, and with replace so are locked layers; with replace the instances are selected → {symbols: [name…], ids: [instance id…] (with replace), skipped: [{layer, name, reason: \"empty\"|\"locked\"}…]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/document.rs"}
  {:id "addon.image.applyColorMask",
   :label "Apply Color Mask",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selected images)} make each image's color mask part of its pixels, as one undo step: the masked pixels become the image's own, embedded as a PNG with an alpha channel (a linked image is embedded), and the mask is taken off; a mask that hides nothing is only taken off (the image keeps its pixels and its link); images without a mask are left as they are (no undo step when none has one), and an object in `ids` that is not an image, and a mask made again for new pixels that would give a grayscale image colorized with a process color an alpha channel, are refused → {changed, ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/mask.rs"}
  {:id "addon.image.colorMask",
   :label "Color Mask…",
   :params
   "{background?: \"edges\" (default: the most common color along the image's edges) | \"corners\" (the average of the image's four corner pixels that are not clear) | \"colors\" (the colors in `colors`), colors?: [color…] or one string of them split by commas or spaces (1 to 16 hex colors or black, white, red, green and blue, as addon.image.removeBackground takes them; needed with background: colors), contiguous?: bool (true: only matching pixels that reach in from an edge are hidden; false: wherever they are; true), match?: \"distance\" (default: a color's RGB distance from a hidden color) | \"channels\" (its largest difference on one of red, green and blue), tolerance?: 0..100 (% as addon.image.removeBackground measures it; a pixel this near a hidden color is hidden; 10), softness?: 0..100 (% past the tolerance over which pixels fade from hidden to shown; 10), ids?: [id…] (default: the selected images)} hide colors of each image without changing its pixels, as one undo step: the image keeps its own pixels, and the mask (these settings, and the image's pixels with the hidden colors made clear, made as Remove Background makes them) is kept with the image and saved with the document; the canvas, printing and separations, PDF, SVG, EPS, raster formats, DXF, EMF, WMF, the legacy .ai and the .ai editing data, copy and paste, and placing a document show the masked pixels, and a click on any part of the image's frame selects it (the Eyedropper, Object Mosaic, Create Gradient Mesh, Crop Image's trim and Image Trace read the image's own pixels); setting the mask again replaces it, and an image whose mask does not change is left as it is (no undo step when none changes); when the image's own pixels are replaced later (Update Link, Relink, Crop Image, a recolor, a linked file read again on open), the mask is made again for the new pixels; an object in `ids` that is not an image, a CMYK image, a linked image that shows its preview (embed or relink it first), an image too large to change, a mask that would hide every pixel, and a mask that would hide pixels of a grayscale image colorized with a process color (masked gray pixels have transparency, which only a spot color, black or white colorizes; each image is checked on the pixels its new mask shows) are refused. With none of background, colors, contiguous, match, tolerance and softness given, nothing changes and the mask settings of the first image (or the defaults when it has no mask) are returned → {changed: the images changed, ids, hidden: the pixels made fully clear in them} or {background, colors, contiguous, match, tolerance, softness, masked}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/mask.rs"}
  {:id "addon.image.removeBackground",
   :label "Remove Background…",
   :params
   "{background?: \"edges\" (default: the most common color along the image's edges; nothing is cleared when the edges hold at least as many clear pixels as pixels of that color) | \"corners\" (the average of the image's four corner pixels that are not clear; nothing is cleared when all four are clear) | \"colors\" (the colors in `colors`), colors?: [color…] or one string of them split by commas or spaces (1 to 16 colors, each a hex color \"#rrggbb\" or \"#rgb\" with or without the # or one of black, white, red, green and blue; needed with background: colors, and checked but not used with edges or corners), contiguous?: bool (true: only background pixels that reach in from an edge are cleared; false: they are cleared wherever they are; true), match?: \"distance\" (default: a color's RGB distance from a background color) | \"channels\" (its largest difference on one of red, green and blue), tolerance?: 0..100 (with distance, % of the largest RGB distance; with channels, % of 255 steps on one channel; a pixel this near a background color is cleared; 10), softness?: 0..100 (% past the tolerance over which pixels fade from cleared to kept; 10), ids?: [id…] (default: the selected images)} make the background of each image transparent in its own pixels, as one undo step: the image stays an image, embedded as a PNG with an alpha channel at the depth of its pixels (16-bit images keep 16 bits and grayscale images stay gray) with the source's color profile and resolution, and a linked image is embedded; a CMYK image, a linked image that shows its preview (embed or relink it first), an image too large to change, a result with no pixel left, and a grayscale image colorized with a process color (which can't colorize gray pixels with transparency) are refused, and an image whose pixels do not change is left as it is (no undo step when none changes) → {changed: the images changed, ids, cleared: the pixels made fully clear in them}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/image.rs"}
  {:id "addon.image.removeColorMask",
   :label "Remove Color Mask",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selected images)} take the color mask off each image, as one undo step: the image shows its own pixels again; images without a mask are left as they are (no undo step when none has one), and an object in `ids` that is not an image is refused → {changed, ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/mask.rs"}
  {:id "addon.packaging.check",
   :label "Check Fold Lines",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selection), select?: bool (false), tolerance?: pt 0.01..10 (0.1)} check the fold lines (addon.packaging.roles) among the objects (through groups and clip groups), or, while nothing is selected and ids is left out, every fold line of the document; hidden lines are left out, also in a selected group. Cut lines bound the blanks: each connected piece of them that encloses material is one blank, its outline is its largest closed cut line, and a closed cut line inside it is a hole, so a slot drawn as a rectangle across the outline leaves the same material as a notch drawn in it; open cut lines that meet end to end count as one closed cut line. Crease, Partial Cut and Perforation lines divide a blank into panels; the pieces of them between two panels are that pair's hinge. A cut line end that comes within tolerance of another cut line is joined to it. Issues, in this order: noCut, open, looseEnd (errors), gap (a warning: the gap is closed), tooComplex (an error: more than 65,536 segments or 256 panels in a blank), cutOverCrease (an error), duplicate (two cut lines, or two lines that fold of any role), danglingCrease, noSplit, outside (wholly, or in part for tolerance or more), notStraight (a hinge's pieces are not on one straight line), sliver, ambiguous, loosePanel (joined to the largest panel by no chain of hinges), nonPrinting (warnings). With select, the objects the issues name become the selection, unless no issue names one. Changes nothing in the document → {ok (no error), blanks, panels, hinges, holes, issues: [{severity: error|warning, code, message (English), ids, at?: [x, y]}], scope: ids|selection|document}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/check.rs"}
  {:id "addon.packaging.setRole",
   :label "Make Fold Line",
   :params
   "{role: cut|crease|partialCut|perforation|none, ids?: [id…] (default: the selection), overprint?: bool (true)} give each path, compound path and live shape among the objects (through groups and clip groups; objects that are locked or hidden, in a locked or hidden group or layer, or on a locked artboard are left out and counted as skipped, even when named in ids) a fold line role: its top stroke is painted with the role's swatch (addon.packaging.roles) at 100% and shown, a path without a stroke gets a 1 pt stroke, and the stroke overprints, or with overprint: false does not. A missing role swatch is made as a global spot swatch (Cut 100% magenta, Crease 100% cyan, Partial Cut 100% yellow, Perforation 50% magenta and 50% cyan, in the document's color mode; named \"Cut 2\" and so on, in the role table too, when a color group or a swatch that can't carry a role, such as a process color that is not global, has the name). none takes the role away: a role stroke keeps the color it shows, no longer linked to the swatch, and stops overprinting. Text, images, symbol instances and other objects are skipped and counted. One undo step, none when nothing changes → {ids (the objects that can carry a role), changed, skipped}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/roles.rs"}
  {:id "addon.packaging.setRoleSwatch",
   :label "Role Swatches…",
   :params
   "{role: cut|crease|partialCut|perforation, swatch: a global or spot color swatch's name} make the swatch carry the role, in the document's role table, as one undo step (none when it already does). Objects stroked with the role's old swatch keep their color and no longer have the role. Refused: a missing swatch, a gradient or pattern swatch, a process color that is not global, a tint swatch, [None], [Registration], and a swatch another role has → {role, swatch, changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/roles.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.addPoints",
   :label "Add Points to Segments…",
   :params
   "{count?: 1..100 (1)} add count anchors to each selected segment (a segment between two selected anchors, or every segment of a path selected whole), splitting it into pieces of equal length; the shape doesn't change. One undo step → {added}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.close",
   :label "Close Path",
   :params
   "{mode?: \"handles\" (keep the ends' handles)|\"straight\" (a straight closing segment)|\"smooth\" (the ends made smooth), ratio?: 0.1..0.5 (0.3905, for smooth)} close the open subpaths of the selected paths, as one undo step → {closed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.commonTangents",
   :label "Common Tangents",
   :params
   "{tangents?: \"external\" (both paths on the same side of each line) | \"internal\" (the lines that run between them) | \"all\" (\"all\"), centerline?: bool (false: true also adds the line joining the two centers, an ellipse's center or a path's center of area), ids?: [id, id] (default: the selection)} add the common tangent lines of two convex closed paths as separate open paths, each from where it touches the first path to where it touches the second (the whole stretch where a straight side lies along it), stroked with the current stroke color and weight (black when the stroke is None) and unfilled, directly above the upper of the two, as one undo step; the new lines are selected. An ellipse drawn with the Ellipse tool, turned or scaled, is measured as an exact ellipse; any other path must be closed, have one outline, bend the same way all around and have at most 10000 segments. Separate paths have two external and two internal tangents; overlapping paths only external ones; one path inside the other has none. Paths that touch, from outside or from inside, share one tangent there instead: a line centered on the point where they touch and as long as the narrower path is wide along it; paths that meet at a corner or along a shared stretch of outline get one such line, at the middle of the directions that touch both. Paths count as touching when the gap between them is less than a billionth of the larger of their sizes and the distance between their centers. When there is no tangent of the kind asked for, nothing changes and the result has a `warning` → {ids, external, internal, centerline (its id or null), warning?}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/tangents.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.corner",
   :label "Make Corner",
   :params
   "{retract?: bool (true: the handles go; false: they stay where they are and move apart)} make the selected anchors corners, as one undo step → {anchors (changed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.cornerRemove",
   :label "Remove Corners",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (the selection), anchors?: [index…] (of each path's outline with no corners cut; else its direct-selected anchors, or all of them), items?: [{id, anchors?}…] (instead of ids: each path with its own anchors)} make those live corners sharp again, as one undo step → {ids, corners (how many)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/corners.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.cornerSet",
   :label "Set Corners",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (the selection), anchors?: [index…] (of each path's outline with no corners cut; else its direct-selected anchors, or all of them), items?: [{id, anchors?}…] (instead of ids: each path with its own anchors), radius: pt 0..1000000 (drawn no larger than fits), kind?: \"round\"|\"invertedRound\"|\"chamfer\" (each corner's own), every?: \"all\"|\"odd\"|\"even\" (default all: of those anchors, only the odd- or even-numbered ones, counting each path's anchors from 1), minAngle?: degrees 0..180 (default 0), maxAngle?: degrees 0..180 (default 180; of those anchors, only the corners whose sides meet at an angle in this range: small for a sharp spike, near 180 for a shallow bend)} cut live corners at the anchors that can have one, as one undo step → {ids, corners (how many)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/corners.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.crossings",
   :label "Add Points at Crossings",
   :params
   "{cut?: bool (false: add anchors where the paths cross; true: also cut them there), selfCrossings?: bool (false: where a path crosses itself too, a curved segment that loops over itself included), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} where the paths under the objects cross one another, as one undo step; at most 10000 segments → {ids, crossings (anchors placed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.divideDashes",
   :label "Divide into Dashes",
   :params
   "{dash?: pt 0.01..1000000 (10), gap?: pt 0..1000000 (0: the pieces touch), fit?: bool (false: exact lengths, the last piece of each run what is left; true: fit to corners and ends, every run between corners and ends holding whole dashes, all stretched or squeezed alike so it starts and ends on a dash), removeGaps?: bool (true: the gaps are left empty; false: they stay as pieces too)} cut the selected paths into separate open paths along the curve, each dash long with gap between them and keeping the path's appearance, as one undo step. Only the direct-selected segments (or those between two direct-selected anchors) are divided when there are any, the dash pattern running on across segments that follow one another; the rest of such a path stays, as pieces of its own. The pieces are selected; at most 100000 → {ids, dashes}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.equalize",
   :label "Equalize Handles",
   :params
   "{} give each selected anchor's two handles their average length (a missing one is made opposite the other), as one undo step → {anchors (changed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.erase",
   :label "Anchor Eraser Brush",
   :params
   "{points: [[x, y] | [x, y, pressure 0..1]…] (the brush's path, at most 100000 points), diameter?: pt 0.1..2500 (20; a point's pressure scales it), tolerance?: 1..100 (10; the outline may move up to tolerance × 0.02 pt), ignoreTolerance?: bool (false: every anchor under the brush that can go goes, its neighbours refitted), plain?: bool (false: true deletes them without refitting the handles beside them), ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} remove the anchors of the paths under the objects that the brush passes over and that can go while the outline stays within the tolerance, as one undo step; open ends stay → {ids, removed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.expandDashes",
   :label "Expand Dashes into Paths",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} turn the dashed stroke of each path and compound path under the objects into separate open paths, one per dash, laid out as the stroke draws them (its dash pattern, offset and Align Dashes to Corners and Path Ends), each keeping the path's appearance with the dashes off, so the gaps are real gaps: a dash running all the way round a closed path stays closed, and with a round or projecting cap a dash of no length (a dot) becomes a path on its point. The top stroke's dashes are the ones expanded; its arrowheads go, and the path's fills stay on it, below its dashes. Paths without a dashed stroke stay as they are. One undo step; the dashes are selected; at most 100000 → {ids, dashes}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.extend",
   :label "Extend Path",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (0), end: \"start\"|\"end\", length?: pt (negative shortens; never all of it), to?: [x, y] (instead of length: the length that brings the end nearest this point), mode?: \"straight\"|\"bezier\" (stretch the last segment's curve, no anchor added)|\"arc\" (along the circle the end curves on, at most half way round) (\"straight\")} lengthen an open path at an end the way it runs there, or shorten it back along itself, as one undo step; with Keep Shared Points Together on, anchors coincident with an end that moves go with it → {id, length (pt)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.mergeEdge",
   :label "Merge Shared Edge",
   :params
   "{a, b: two path ids (they needn't be selected), at: [x, y] (where), diameter?: pt 0.25..200 (20; how near `at` the edge is looked for), tolerance?: pt 0..3 (0.002; how near two anchors count as coincident), follow?: \"average\" (half way between the two)|\"a\"|\"b\" (keep that path's outline), ends?: bool (false: true makes an end even where the paths could merge)} where the paths touch at two coincident anchors, one each side of `at`, replace the stretches between them with one shared edge; stretches much longer one than the other (by over 10%) or leaving an end at over 120° aren't merged. Otherwise make an end there: two near anchors meet, and an anchor only one path has there is matched by a new one on the other. Each path stays closed or open; one undo step → {a, b, made: \"edge\"|\"end\"|\"nothing\" (merged already)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shared_edge.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.movePointsTogether",
   :label "Keep Shared Points Together",
   :params
   "{enabled?: bool (default: the opposite of now)} Keep Shared Points Together: whether anchors coincident (within the Shared Edge Merge Tool's `tolerance`) with one that Slide Anchor Along Path, Extend Path or Set Anchor moves move with it, on any editable path (the `together` option of tool `sharedEdge`, kept with the preferences; off by default) → {enabled}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shared_edge.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.removeKeepShape",
   :label "Remove Points, Keep Shape",
   :params
   "{} remove the direct-selected anchors, refitting the handles beside each so the outline keeps its shape as best it can, as one undo step; open ends stay → {removed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.setAnchor",
   :label "Set Anchor",
   :params
   "{x?, y?: pt (on the page), inLength?, outLength?: pt (0 retracts), inAngle?, outAngle?: degrees counter-clockwise} move the selected anchors (with their handles) and set their handles, as one undo step: direct-selected anchors, or every anchor of a path selected whole; a smooth anchor's other handle turns with the one set; with Keep Shared Points Together on, anchors coincident with one that moves go with it → {anchors}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.shape.convert",
   :label "Convert to Parametric Shape",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selection)} make each plain closed path that is a rectangle, an ellipse or a polygon with equal sides and corners (stretched along its own axes at most) a parametric shape of the same outline, as one undo step → {ids (converted)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shape.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.shape.create",
   :label "Parametric Shape",
   :params
   "{center: [x, y], kind?: \"rectangle\"|\"ellipse\"|\"polygon\" (default)|\"star\"|\"ring\"|\"arrow\"|\"cross\"|\"heart\"|\"gear\"|\"bubble\" (a speech bubble), width?, height?: 0.01..16384 pt (100), rotation?: degrees clockwise (0: upright), count?: 3..1000 (a polygon's sides, a star's points, a gear's teeth), a?, b?: the kind's own values (star: inner radius 0.01..1 of the outer, 0.5; ring: hole 0.01..0.99 of the size, 0.5; arrow: head length and shaft width 0.05..0.95, 0.4 and 0.4; cross: bar offset −0.9..0.9 (0, − up) and arm thickness 0.05..0.95 (1/3); heart: notch depth and point roundness 0..1 (0.4 and 0); gear: tooth height 0.01..0.9 (0.2); bubble: tail height 0.05..0.9 (0.25) and tail tip −1..1 across (−0.4)), radius?: corner radius 0..16384 pt (0; no corner rounds past the middle of a side)} draw a parametric shape with the current paint, selected, as one undo step; it stays editable with addon.pathtools.shape.set until its anchors are edited (moving, turning or scaling it keeps it) → {id, shape}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shape.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.shape.set",
   :label "Edit Parametric Shape",
   :params
   "{id, kind?, center?, width?, height?, rotation?: degrees clockwise (0: upright), count?, a?, b?, radius?} change a parametric shape's numbers (as addon.pathtools.shape.create takes them; a new kind takes its own defaults for the values not given), as one undo step; with none, or the same ones, nothing changes → {id, shape (its numbers now)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shape.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.slideAnchor",
   :label "Slide Anchor Along Path",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (0), anchor: index, t: -0.98..0.98 (where to: positive, a curve parameter on the segment after the anchor; negative, back from the end of the one before)} move an anchor along its path, the segments beside it refitted so the outline stays, as one undo step; ends of open paths don't slide; with Keep Shared Points Together on, anchors coincident with it go with it → {id, strayed (pt)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.smooth",
   :label "Make Smooth",
   :params
   "{ratio?: 0.1..0.5 (0.3905: a square's corners make a circle)} make the selected anchors smooth: a lone handle is mirrored; without handles, both stand at right angles to the bisector of the angle at the anchor, ratio × the nearer neighbour's distance long; two handles are put in line; an open end without handles aims at its neighbour's handle. One undo step → {anchors (changed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pathtools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.tangentCircle",
   :label "Tangent Circle",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (two or three paths or compound paths; default: the selection), radius?: pt 0.01..1000000 (needed with two shapes; three shapes set the radius themselves and take none), circle?: 0..64 (0: every circle found; n: only the nth, the circles listed by radius, then top to bottom, then left to right)} draw the circles that touch two shapes and have the radius, or that touch three shapes. A circle touches a shape when it meets the shape's outline without crossing it, the whole outline lying outside the circle or inside it: it is tangent to the outline at a smooth point and passes through a corner or an open end; the members of a compound path count as one outline. With three shapes, circles up to 64 times the diagonal of the box around the shapes' anchors and handles are found. Each circle is a new ellipse with the current paint on top of the current layer, or of the isolated group (inside an isolated compound path they join it); the circles are selected; one undo step. Locked and hidden shapes given by `ids` are read and left as they are. No circle is an error, and so are more than 64 (shapes touched along a whole curve, such as two concentric circles), an object named twice, shapes at one point or too small for the radius, and more than 2000 segments in all; the document is then unchanged → {ids, found (how many circles touch the shapes)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/tangent_circle.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pathtools.trim",
   :label "Trim at Crossings",
   :params
   "{at: [x, y], tolerance?: pt 0..100 (3; how near `at` a path counts as under it)} or {rect: [x, y, width, height]} or {points: [[x, y]…] (2 to 100000 points)} remove stretches of paths, a stretch running between two neighboring places where the path is crossed by another path or by itself, or from such a place to an open end: `at` removes the stretch of the nearest path at that point, `rect` every stretch the rectangle touches, `points` every stretch the line through the points crosses. Give exactly one of the three. Every path that can be edited takes part, selected or not, compound path members included; hidden and locked paths, guides and clipping paths (compound ones' members included) are neither trimmed nor counted as crossing; in isolation mode only paths inside the isolated object are trimmed. A path that ends on another marks a place on the other; paths that lie along each other don't cross. A closed path that loses a stretch becomes open, an open path that loses a middle stretch becomes two paths with its appearance in its place in the stacking order, and a path nothing crosses is removed whole; a live shape becomes a plain path. One undo step, none when nothing is removed → {ids (the paths left of those trimmed), removed (stretches)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/trim.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.append",
   :label "Smart Pen",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (default: the last open subpath), x, y, in?: [x, y], out?: [x, y], segment?: \"straight\" (the segment into the new anchor is a line: the previous anchor's handle on it goes, and the new anchor's incoming one)|\"curved\" (the previous anchor gets a handle on it if it has none: in line with its other handle, or with a straight segment before it)} add an anchor at the end of an open subpath of path id (default: the handles as given, the previous anchor as it is), as one undo step; the new anchor is selected → {anchor}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.close",
   :label "Close Path",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (default: the last open subpath), segment?: \"straight\"|\"curved\" (default: the closing segment takes the handles its ends have)} close an open subpath of two anchors or more, as one undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.closeJoin",
   :label "Close or Join",
   :params
   "{} with exactly two open path ends direct-selected, join them as path.join does; else close the selected open paths keeping their ends' handles, as addon.pathtools.close does. One undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.nextSegment",
   :label "Next Segment",
   :params
   "{curved: bool} whether a click with the Smart Pen Tool adds a curved segment or a straight one (the tool's `next` option, kept with the preferences) → {next: \"straight\"|\"curved\"}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.removePoint",
   :label "Remove Points, Keep Shape",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (0), anchor: index, plain?: bool (false: the handles beside it are refitted so the outline keeps its shape, and an open end takes its segment with it; true: it goes and the handles beside it stay as they are)} remove one anchor, as one undo step; a subpath keeps two anchors (three when closed)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.reshape",
   :label "Reshape Segment",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (0), segment: index, t?: 0..1 (where it was grabbed, 0.5; held to 0.05..0.95), dx, dy: pt, mode?: \"free\" (both handles move, the one nearer the grab more)|\"keepAngles\" (each handle keeps its direction)|\"symmetric\" (both handles at right angles to the chord, at one length) (\"free\")} bend a segment so the point grabbed moves by (dx, dy); missing handles grow out of their anchors and a smooth anchor stays smooth. One undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.segment",
   :label "Straight or Curved Segment",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (0), segment: index, curved: bool} make a segment straight (its handles retracted) or curved (each end without a handle on it gets one, in line with its other handle or with a straight segment before it), as one undo step → {changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.pen.togglePoint",
   :label "Convert Anchor Point",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?: index (0), anchor: index, ratio?: 0.1..0.5 (0.3905)} a smooth anchor becomes a corner with its handles where they are; any other anchor is made smooth by the auto-smooth rule (a lone handle mirrored; without handles both at right angles to the bisector of the angle at it, ratio × the nearer neighbour's distance long). One undo step → {smooth}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/pen.rs"}
  {:id "addon.select.byArtboards",
   :label "Select by Artboards",
   :params
   "{artboards: [index…] (0-based whole numbers, at least one), relation?: \"overlap\" (default: on at least one of them, as select.allOnArtboard takes it: the bounds overlap the artboard or the centre is on it) | \"inside\" (the bounds lie wholly within one of them, edges included) | \"outside\" (on none of them)} select those objects among the ones Select All takes (in isolation mode, the isolated container's); hidden and locked objects, objects on hidden, locked or template layers and art held by a locked artboard are left out. Bounds are geometric, a symbol instance's measured by its art → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/select.rs"}
  {:id "addon.select.byLinkStatus",
   :label "Select by Link Status",
   :params
   "{status: \"linked\" (its file found unchanged) | \"embedded\" | \"missing\" | \"modified\" (its file changed since it was read) | [several of them] (at least one), ids?: [object ids] (pick only among these; default: every image and placed document in the layers), add?: false (add to the selection instead of replacing it), zoom?: false (then zoom to the selection: the desktop app runs addon.arrange.zoomSelection when something was selected; elsewhere the result's zoom flag asks the caller to)} select the image objects and placed documents whose link has that status, as links.list reports it. Those that are hidden or locked, inside a hidden or locked object or layer, on a template layer, on a locked artboard while nothing is isolated, or outside the isolated group or layer are left out and listed with the reason. Only the selection changes, not the document → {count (how many it selected), selected: [ids] (in stacking order, bottom first), skipped: [{id, reason: hidden|locked|template|isolation}], zoom?: true}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/select.rs"}
  {:id "addon.shapes.box3d",
   :label "3D Box",
   :params
   "{x, y, width, height: pt (0 or more), angleX=30 (degrees about the level axis: positive tips the top away from you), angleY=30 (degrees about the upright axis: positive turns the right side away from you), angleZ=0 (degrees clockwise in the page), parallelX=false, parallelY=true, parallelZ=false} → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shapes.rs"}
  {:id "addon.shapes.configure",
   :label "Configure Shape",
   :params
   "{ids?, radius?: pt (0 or more; fitted to half each rectangle's shorter side), radii?: [tl,tr,br,bl] (each 0 or more), startAngle?, endAngle?: degrees (as addon.shapes.rectangle, ellipse, polygon and star take them: an ellipse's counter-clockwise from 3 o'clock, the others' clockwise along the outline), arcMode?: whole|pie|chord|arc, sides?: a whole number 3 to 1000, isStar?, spokeRatio?: 0.01 to 1, rounded?, randomized?: -10 to 10, turns?: 0.01 to 1024, divergence?: 0 to 1000, innerRadius?: 0 to 0.999, angleX?, angleY?: degrees (as addon.shapes.box3d: positive tips the top, or turns the right side, away from you), angleZ?: degrees clockwise in the page, parallelX?, parallelY?, parallelZ?, reset?: bool} an omitted or null value keeps each shape's setting → {updated}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shapes.rs"}
  {:id "addon.shapes.ellipse",
   :label "Ellipse",
   :params
   "{x, y, width, height: pt (0 or more), startAngle?, endAngle?: degrees (counter-clockwise from 3 o'clock, as object.setLiveShape's pieStart and pieEnd; default 0 and 360), arcMode?: whole|pie|chord|arc, rotation?: deg clockwise about the centre (0: upright)} → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shapes.rs"}
  {:id "addon.shapes.polygon",
   :label "Polygon",
   :params
   "{cx, cy, radius: pt (0 or more), sides=6: a whole number 3 to 1000, rounded=0, randomized=0: -10 to 10, startAngle?, endAngle?: degrees (the part of the outline kept, clockwise from its first anchor, the top corner; each side an equal share of 360; default 0 and 360), arcMode?: whole|pie|chord|arc, rotation?: deg clockwise (0: a corner straight up)} → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shapes.rs"}
  {:id "addon.shapes.rectangle",
   :label "Rectangle",
   :params
   "{x, y, width, height: pt (0 or more), radius?: pt (0 or more), radii?: [tl,tr,br,bl] (each 0 or more), startAngle?, endAngle?: degrees (the part of the outline kept, clockwise from its first anchor, the top-left corner; each side an equal share of 360; default 0 and 360), arcMode?: whole|pie|chord|arc, rotation?: deg clockwise about the centre (0: upright)} → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shapes.rs"}
  {:id "addon.shapes.spiral",
   :label "Spiral",
   :params
   "{cx, cy, radius: pt (0 or more), turns=3: 0.01 to 1024, divergence=1: 0 to 1000, innerRadius=0: 0 to 0.999 of radius, clockwise=true} → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shapes.rs"}
  {:id "addon.shapes.star",
   :label "Star",
   :params
   "{cx, cy, radius1: pt (0 or more), radius2?: pt (0.01 to 1 times radius1; default half of it), points=5: a whole number 3 to 1000, rounded=0, randomized=0: -10 to 10, startAngle?, endAngle?: degrees (the part of the outline kept, clockwise from its first anchor, the top point; each side an equal share of 360; default 0 and 360), arcMode?: whole|pie|chord|arc, rotation?: deg clockwise (0: a point straight up)} → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shapes.rs"}
  {:id "addon.type.releasePath",
   :label "Release Type on a Path…",
   :params
   "{mode?: \"both\" (point type and the path) | \"path\" (the path only) | \"text\" (point type only) (\"both\"), keepOriginal?: false (true: the type on a path stays and the released objects go just above it), ids?: [id…], id? (instead of ids; neither: the selection)} split each type on a path among the objects (inside groups too) into point type and the path it was set on. The point type holds the same text with the same character and paragraph attributes, on one straight line whose baseline starts where the first character sat on the path (when the type starts before an open path's start, the first character drawn on the path stays where it was drawn and the characters that were not drawn come before it); Type on a Path Options (effect, align to path, spacing, flip, brackets) don't apply to point type and are dropped; type with Dynamic Text on (type.dynamicText) comes out with it off, at the sizes it was drawn at. The path keeps its exact shape (open or closed, anchors and handles, the object's transform) and comes out with no fill and no stroke, in the type's layer and place in the stacking order. Other objects are left alone, and with no type on a path among them nothing changes and no undo step is made. One undo step; the released objects are selected → {ids (released, bottom to top), paths, texts}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/typetools.rs"}
  {:id "addon.type.textTweaker",
   :label "Text Tweaker",
   :params
   "{attribute?: \"size\" (pt 0.1..1296) | \"baselineShift\" (pt −1296..1296) | \"rotation\" (° −360..360) | \"hScale\" (% 1..10000) | \"vScale\" (% 1..10000) | \"tracking\" (1/1000 em −1000..10000) | \"leading\" (pt 0.1..5000) | \"strokeWidth\" (pt 0..1000) (\"size\"), from?: the first character's value, to?: the last character's value (each in the attribute's units and range; defaults: size 12 → 36, baselineShift 0 → 12, rotation 0 → 30, hScale and vScale 100 → 150, tracking 0 → 200, leading 12 → 36, strokeWidth 0 → 2), shape?: \"straight\" (an even ramp) | \"ease\" (slow at both ends) | \"bow\" (from at both ends, rising smoothly to `to` in the middle) | \"spike\" (from at both ends, straight up to `to` in the middle) | \"random\" (each character anywhere from `from` to `to`) (\"straight\"), seed?: whole number (0; random: the same seed and text give the same values), skipSpaces?: true (spaces and line breaks keep their values and don't count), id?, start?: byte, end?: byte (range endpoints inside a character round down to its start), ids?: [id…] (instead of id)} give the characters one character attribute letter by letter, from `from` to `to` along the shape, as the Character panel sets it, as one undo step; the text stays live and editable. The range of `id`, else the type objects in `ids`, else the text the Type tool has selected (at a caret: all its text), else every selected type object; each object gets its own ramp. Stroke weight only shows on characters with a stroke → {count (characters changed), ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/typetools.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.addEffect",
   :label "Add Effect",
   :params
   "{…as effect.apply} same as effect.apply (an alias): {effect: id, params?: {…}, item?: appearance item index|null, ids?, target?, aligned?} → {ids, index, item}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.addFill",
   :label "Add New Fill",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, target?: \"object\"|\"contents\"} add a fill on top of each selected object's own stack, on an image right below its Contents row, with its top fill's paint (type without one: its characters' fill; else the default fill). With a fill row active (appearance.setActiveItem), no `ids`, no `id` and no `target: \"contents\"`, the new fill takes that row's paint, goes right above it, and becomes the active row; appearance.duplicateItem copies a whole row. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, what the edit changes, and the row it adds when that row becomes the line's topmost visible row of its kind)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.addStroke",
   :label "Add New Stroke",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, target?} add a stroke on top of each selected object's own stack, on an image right below its Contents row, with its top stroke's paint (else the default stroke) and that stroke's weight when it has paint, at least 1 pt. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, what the edit changes, and the row it adds when that row becomes the line's topmost visible row of its kind)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.clear",
   :label "Clear Appearance",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, target?} leave each object one empty fill and stroke (None; a group none of its own) and reset its opacity and blend mode. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths and the group), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke and the object's opacity and blend mode (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.copyFrom",
   :label "Eyedropper",
   :params
   "{source: id, ids?, pickUp?, apply? (trees as eyedropper.setOptions, merged over the Eyedropper Options for this call), reverse?: bool, append?: bool, defaultsOnly?: bool} copy the attributes both picked up and applied (by default the whole appearance stack, opacity and blend mode, and from type to type the character and paragraph attributes using effective character dimensions while preserving target transforms) from `source` to ids (default: highlighted characters while editing type, after Select All in a frame of threaded text the text of the story's frames, leaving out `source`, otherwise the object selection; highlighted characters reject enabled non-neutral object transparency), the fill, stroke and weight also to the paint defaults; `defaultsOnly` updates only paint defaults and cannot be combined with ids, reverse or append; `reverse` (Alt-click) copies from the first selected object (or ids) onto `source` instead, or with nothing selected what the Eyedropper picked up last (a click without Alt); `append` (Shift+Alt-click) adds the source's fills, strokes and effects on top of each target's stack; placed gradients land at the same place relative to each target's bounds (defaults: fitted to new art); with an object of a dynamic symbol instance selected by Direct Selection and no ids, reverse, append or defaultsOnly, that object takes the source's fill and stroke (solid, none, gradient or pattern) for this instance only, as the Eyedropper Options allow, and a source that is not a path, compound path or type, or options that pick up neither color, are refused. On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke and the object's opacity and blend mode (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, the graph stores, for every label of its kind, the character attributes the pick gives all of its text, its object opacity and blend mode when transparency is applied, and with `append` its topmost visible fill and stroke rows of the kinds it adds; on a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring, its topmost visible fill and stroke rows, and when transparency is applied its object opacity and blend mode, for every line of its kind (a pick of some attributes without `append`: what it changes, and the paint, stroke weight and row transparency it applies to the topmost visible rows; with `append`: only the kinds of row it adds) → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.duplicateItem",
   :label "Duplicate Item",
   :params
   "{index | indices: [..] (paint-order item indices), to?: paint-order index of the copy (with several, of the lowest copy: they land together in their order; default: each right above its item; not with aligned rows of a mixed selection), contents?: count (with `to`: how many items paint below the Contents (Characters) row afterwards; default: it stays between the same items), ids?|id?, target?, aligned?: bool (index and item are rows of the first target's stack: each other target edits its equal one, as the Appearance panel does for a mixed selection; with the art of a graph design in a series given first, rows of the art's stack: docs/mcp.md)} copy fills/strokes with their effects, as Alt-dragging rows places them. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels; when their rows differ, the indices need `aligned` and are rows of the backmost one), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, only what the edit changes)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.moveItem",
   :label "Reorder Appearance Item",
   :params
   "{from: paint-order item index | \"contents\", indices?: [..] (several items instead of from: they move as one block in their order, the lowest landing at `to`; a block landing next to the Contents row keeps its lowest item's side), to, contents?: count, ids?|id?, target?, aligned?: bool (refused when the targets' appearances differ, or differ from that of a graph design's art given first)} move fill/stroke `from` to paint-order index `to`; on a group, layer or type the Contents (Characters) row stays between the same items (a moved item landing next to it keeps its side) unless `contents` says how many items paint below it afterwards. from \"contents\": move that row so `to` items paint below the members (characters) and the rest above. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths, except with from \"contents\", which moves the group's own row), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels; moving rows of such a group whose members' rows differ is an error), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, only what the edit changes) → {index: where the item landed | contents: the row's slot}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.reduceToBasic",
   :label "Reduce to Basic Appearance",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, target?} keep only one visible fill and stroke (without ids: the Appearance panel's active row in place of the topmost one of its kind; else the topmost), without their own opacity, blend mode or effects (a group keeps no rows it lacked), and drop the object's effects. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths and the group), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, only what the edit changes)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.removeItem",
   :label "Remove Item",
   :params
   "{index | indices: [..] (paint-order item indices), ids?|id?, target?, aligned?: bool (index and item are rows of the first target's stack: each other target edits its equal one, as the Appearance panel does for a mixed selection; with the art of a graph design in a series given first, rows of the art's stack: docs/mcp.md)} remove those fills/strokes from each target object's own stack. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels; when their rows differ, the indices need `aligned` and are rows of the backmost one), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, only what the edit changes)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.setActiveItem",
   :label "Select Appearance Item",
   :params
   "{index: paint-order item index in the first selected object's stack | null} make that fill/stroke row the target of the paint.setFill/setStroke, stroke.set/setAdvanced, paint.editGradient/setGradientGeom, transparency.set and effect.* calls that omit `item` (a fill row brings the Fill proxy forward, a stroke row the Stroke proxy); null or any selection change clears it → {index}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.setItem",
   :label "Appearance Item",
   :params
   "{index: paint-order item index, ids?|id? (default: the selection), target?: \"object\"|\"contents\", opacity?: 0..100, blend?: name, visible?: bool, weight?: pt (strokes), color?|none?|swatch?|gradient? (as paint.setFill), tint?: 0..100, keepModel?: bool (both as paint.setFill), aligned?: bool (index and item are rows of the first target's stack: each other target edits its equal one, as the Appearance panel does for a mixed selection; with the art of a graph design in a series given first, rows of the art's stack: docs/mcp.md)} edit one fill/stroke of each target object's own appearance stack. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels; when their rows differ, `index` needs `aligned` and is a row of the backmost one), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, what the edit changes, and the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode it writes to the line's topmost visible row)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.setNewArtBasic",
   :label "New Art Has Basic Appearance",
   :params
   "{on?: bool (omitted: toggle)} the Appearance panel option (the preference newArtBasic, on by default): on, new art takes one fill and stroke (with the Stroke panel's options), the fill, stroke and weight the selection shares when it last changed; off, the whole appearance of the last selected object (every fill, stroke and effect, opacity and blend mode) → {on}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/newart.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.showAllHidden",
   :label "Show All Hidden Attributes",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, target?} make every hidden fill, stroke and effect (the object's and each item's) of each selected object visible again; errors when nothing is hidden. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths and the group), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind (of a line, only what the edit changes) → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.targetContents",
   :label "Target Contents",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, target?: \"object\"|\"contents\"} select the members of the selected groups and layers (or `ids`), as double-clicking the Appearance panel's Contents row does: the panel then lists, and appearance edits change, their own appearance; errors when none has members → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "appearance.transfer",
   :label "Move Appearance",
   :params
   "{source: id, target: id, copy?: bool} give `target` (a layer, group or object) the appearance (fills, strokes, effects) and transparency (opacity, blend mode, isolation, knockout) of `source`, as dragging a target circle onto another in the Layers panel does; the source is left with a cleared appearance (as appearance.clear) unless `copy` (Alt-drag). Opacity masks stay; placed gradients keep their place relative to each object's bounds. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths; as `source`, when the group has no effect, opacity, blend mode, isolation, knockout or style link of its own, the topmost one is read and a move clears them all; as `target` each takes the appearance and the group is cleared, a `source` among them keeps its look, and a `source` that is the group's only path is an error), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke and the object's opacity and blend mode (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind → {source, target}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/appearance.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.align",
   :label "Align",
   :params
   "{index? | indices?: [n…], selectedArtboards?: [n…] (as artboard.duplicate; default: the artboards the Artboard tool has selected, else its active one), horizontal?: \"left\"|\"center\"|\"right\", vertical?: \"top\"|\"center\"|\"bottom\" (one of the two is needed), to?: \"selection\"|\"artboard\" (default \"selection\": the bounds of the artboards together; \"artboard\": artboard `artboard`, which stays where it is), artboard?: n (0-based; the artboard to align to with to: \"artboard\"; default: the Artboard tool's active one; it need not be one of the artboards aligned), activeArtboard?: n (the journal records that default here, for a replay; `artboard` goes ahead of it), moveArt?: bool (the art fully inside each artboard moves with it, art inside two of them with the first by index, which may stay; default: the Artboard tool's Move Artwork with Artboard option), patterns?: bool, lockedAndHidden?: bool (as artboard.move)} (Align panel › Align Objects with the Artboard tool chosen) each artboard moves until its edge or center is on that edge or center of what it aligns to, with its guides, in one undo step; a locked artboard stays where it is and still counts in the bounds, and the call fails with `the artboard is locked` when every artboard it names is locked; when no artboard moves, no undo step is recorded → {moved: [index…]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/artboardalign.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.convertToArtboards",
   :label "Convert to Artboards",
   :params
   "{} turn each selected object's bounds into a new artboard (the objects are removed) → {artboards}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/menucmds.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.copy",
   :label "Copy Artboard",
   :params
   "{index? | indices?, selectedArtboards?, art?, lockedAndHidden?} (defaults as artboard.duplicate) put the artboards, and the art fully inside each when `art`, on the clipboard: edit.paste adds a copy of each, together right of the last artboard as they lay, edit.pasteInPlace/InFront/InBack where they were, in this or another document (one undo step; edit.pasteOnAllArtboards pastes only the art); edit.copy runs this while the Artboard tool is chosen → {copied: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/panelcmds.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.cut",
   :label "Cut Artboard",
   :params
   "{index? | indices?, selectedArtboards?, art?, lockedAndHidden?} artboard.copy, then delete the artboards and that art in one undo step (one artboard is always left: the cut fails when it names every artboard, or a locked one; art also on another locked artboard stays, and is left off the clipboard, unless lockedAndHidden); edit.cut runs this while the Artboard tool is chosen → {copied: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/panelcmds.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.delete",
   :label "Delete Artboard",
   :params
   "{index | indices: [index…]} delete artboards (with their guides) in one step; one is always left, and a locked one is an error",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.deleteEmpty",
   :label "Delete Empty Artboards",
   :params
   "{} delete every artboard with no artwork on it (no object, hidden, locked and template art included, whose visual bounds meet or touch it, clip groups and clipping layers by their members inside the clip; guides don't count), with its guides, in one step; locked artboards stay; when every artboard is empty and none is locked, artboard 1 stays (with a locked one left, artboard 1 can go) → {deleted: [index…]} (the indices before deleting)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.distribute",
   :label "Distribute",
   :params
   "{index? | indices?, selectedArtboards? (as artboard.align), horizontal?: \"left\"|\"center\"|\"right\" | vertical?: \"top\"|\"center\"|\"bottom\" (one is needed; horizontal goes first), to?: \"selection\"|\"artboard\", artboard?: n, activeArtboard?: n (as artboard.align; with `spacing` the artboard must be one of those distributed), spacing?: pt (used with to: \"artboard\"), moveArt?, patterns?, lockedAndHidden? (as artboard.align)} (Align panel › Distribute Objects with the Artboard tool chosen) the named edges or centers of the artboards are spaced evenly between the first and the last along the axis, which stay where they are (three or more artboards); with to: \"artboard\", the artboards are spaced the same way and then moved together so that artboard `artboard`, when it is one of them, stays where it is; with to: \"artboard\" and `spacing`, that artboard stays and the edges or centers are placed `spacing` apart, outward from it in their order (two or more); a locked artboard stays where it is and keeps its place in the order, and the call fails with `the artboard is locked` when every artboard it names is locked; a spacing that would move an artboard past the canvas is an error; with fewer artboards, or when none moves, no undo step is recorded → {moved: [index…]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/artboardalign.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.distributeSpacing",
   :label "Distribute Spacing",
   :params
   "{index? | indices?, selectedArtboards? (as artboard.align), axis?: \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\" (default horizontal), to?: \"selection\"|\"artboard\", artboard?: n, activeArtboard?: n (as artboard.distribute), spacing?: pt (used with to: \"artboard\"), moveArt?, patterns?, lockedAndHidden? (as artboard.align)} (Align panel › Distribute Spacing with the Artboard tool chosen) the gaps between the artboards along the axis become equal, the first and the last staying where they are (three or more artboards); with to: \"artboard\", the gaps become equal the same way and the artboards then move together so that artboard `artboard`, when it is one of them, stays where it is; with to: \"artboard\" and `spacing`, that artboard stays and the others are placed with a gap of `spacing` between neighbors (two or more; a negative spacing overlaps them); a locked artboard stays where it is and keeps its place in the order, and the call fails with `the artboard is locked` when every artboard it names is locked; a spacing that would move an artboard past the canvas is an error; with fewer artboards, or when none moves, no undo step is recorded → {moved: [index…]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/artboardalign.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.duplicate",
   :label "Duplicate Artboard",
   :params
   "{index?: n | indices?: [n…] (default: the artboards the Artboard tool has selected), selectedArtboards?: [n…] (the journal records that default here, for a replay), art?: bool (default: the Artboard tool's moveArt option), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles), lockedAndHidden?: bool (locked and hidden art goes too; default: prefs moveLockedWithArtboard), side?: \"left\"|\"right\"|\"top\"|\"bottom\" (the copies go together on that side of the artboards they copy, 20 pt away)} a copy of each artboard, the copies placed together right of the last artboard as they lay (or on `side`), with copies of the art fully inside each when `art`, in one undo step → {index: the first copy's index, indices: the copies' indices, ids: the art's copies}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/panelcmds.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.fitToArt",
   :label "Fit to Artwork Bounds",
   :params
   "{index?: n | indices?: [n…] (0-based; the app passes the selected artboards: the Artboard tool's, else the active one; default: the first)} each artboard fits the art on it that shows (with its strokes and effects; hidden objects and layers, guides and template layers don't count), in one undo step (none when every artboard already fits): an object counts for every artboard its bounds overlap, and a group or clipping layer counts as one object; an artboard with no art, or a locked one, stays as it is, and the command fails when every artboard it names is locked or none has art",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.fitToSelection",
   :label "Fit to Selected Art",
   :params
   "{index?: n (0-based; the app passes the active artboard; default: the first)} the artboard fits the selected art (with its strokes); a locked artboard stays as it is (an error when the fit would change it)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.move",
   :label "Move Artboard",
   :params
   "{index | indices: [index…], dx, dy, moveArt?: bool, copy?: bool, patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles), lockedAndHidden?: bool (default: prefs moveLockedWithArtboard)} move artboards (and the art fully inside them; locked and hidden art, and art also on another locked artboard, only with lockedAndHidden), several in one step (an error when one is locked); `copy` (Alt-drag) leaves them and moves copies, which start unlocked → {index (the first), indices: the artboards moved or the copies, moved: the art moved or the copies}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/xform.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.new",
   :label "New Artboard",
   :params
   "{x?, y?, width?, height? (each more than 0 and at most 3,999,856 pt, as file.new takes them), name?, color?: color (its background color, as artboard.setProps takes it, #rrggbbaa and #rgba refused; default: none), guideLabel?: name | \"#rrggbb\" | null (its guide label, as artboard.setProps takes it; default: none), showCenterMark?: bool, showCrossHairs?: bool, showVideoSafeAreas?: bool (as artboard.setProps takes them; default false), videoRulerPixelAspectRatio?: number 0.1–10 (as artboard.setProps takes it; default 1), side?: \"left\"|\"right\"|\"top\"|\"bottom\" (the size of artboard `beside`, 20 pt from that side of it; refused with x, y, width or height), beside?: n (the artboard `side` places it by; default the last)} (default place: right of the last)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.rearrange",
   :label "Rearrange All Artboards…",
   :params
   "{layout?: gridByRow|gridByColumn|row|column (gridByRow; byColumn?: true is gridByColumn), order?: leftToRight|rightToLeft (leftToRight: right-to-left mirrors the order along the rows), columns?: n (2; the rows for gridByColumn; row and column ignore it), spacing?: pt (20), moveArtwork?: true (each object of a layer or sublayer moves with the artboard its center is on; locked and hidden art, and art on a locked artboard, only with lockedAndHidden), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles), lockedAndHidden?: bool (default: prefs moveLockedWithArtboard), byColumn?: bool (an older way to ask for layout gridByColumn)} lay the artboards out in their order, the grid's top-left at the first artboard's; a locked artboard stays where it is → {artboards, rows, columns}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/menucmds.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.rename",
   :label "Rename Artboards",
   :params
   "{index? | indices?, selectedArtboards?: [n…] (as artboard.duplicate), name} (default: the artboards the Artboard tool has selected, else its active one) rename the artboards in one undo step: one takes `name` (trimmed), and several take it numbered in artboard order, `name-1`, `name-2` and so on; a locked artboard is renamed too. An empty name is an error, and when every artboard already has its new name nothing changes and no undo step is recorded → {renamed: [index…]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/panelcmds.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.reorder",
   :label "Move Artboard Up/Down",
   :params "{index, to} change an artboard's number",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/panelcmds.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.setProps",
   :label "Artboard Options…",
   :params
   "{index | artboards: [{index, name?, color?, guideLabel?, locked?, showCenterMark?, showCrossHairs?, showVideoSafeAreas?, videoRulerPixelAspectRatio?, x?, y?, width?, height?}…] (several artboards in one undo step, each with its own fields; the art inside each before any of them changes goes with it, and an object inside several goes with the first listed that moves or scales its art), name?, color?: color (\"#rrggbb\", {c,m,y,k}, … as the paint commands take, #rrggbbaa and #rgba refused: the background color the canvas draws the artboard's paper in, multiplied with the Simulate Colored Paper color while that is on; exports and print leave it out) | null (no background color), guideLabel?: name | \"#rrggbb\" | null (the guide label: the canvas draws the artboard's own guides (guide.add with artboard) in this color instead of the guide color preference, selected ones still in the selection color; a layer color's name spelled exactly as Layer Options lists it (\"Light Blue\", \"Red\", …) or #rrggbb; null for none, which new artboards and older files have; screen-only, so exports and print leave it out; it can change on a locked artboard; an invalid value anywhere in the list changes nothing), locked?: bool (the Artboards panel's lock column: a locked artboard keeps its rectangle (a new x, y, width or height is an error unless locked is false), can't be moved, deleted or cut, and Rearrange and Fit to Artwork Bounds leave it as it is; the art on it (each object of a layer or sublayer whose bounds with strokes overlap it, a group as one object) acts as locked art until it is unlocked: clicks, marquees, select.set, select.all and the tools pass over it (art drawn or pasted onto it stays selected and editable until a selection leaves it out or it is moved off the locked artboards), it is deselected, and when another artboard moves or scales it stays unless lockedAndHidden), showCenterMark?: bool (Artboard Options' Show Center Mark: the canvas draws a mark at the artboard's center), showCrossHairs?: bool (Show Cross Hairs: the canvas draws a line from the middle of each side through the center), showVideoSafeAreas?: bool (Show Video Safe Areas: the canvas draws the action-safe area 3.5% and the title-safe area 5% in from each edge, as EBU R 95 sets them; the three are screen-only, as the artboard's edges are: exports and print leave them out), videoRulerPixelAspectRatio?: number 0.1–10 (Video Ruler Pixel Aspect Ratio: the width of one video pixel over its height, which View › Rulers › Show Video Rulers counts the artboard in; default 1, square pixels), x?, y?, width?, height?, moveArt?: bool (default false; a position-only change moves the contained art with its artboard), scaleArt?: bool (Scale Artwork with Artboard: resized, the artboard takes the art fully inside it (locked and hidden art only with lockedAndHidden?: bool, default prefs moveLockedWithArtboard) and its guides from its old rectangle onto the new one, each side by its own ratio; strokes/corners/patterns as object.scale), strokes?: bool, corners?: bool, patterns?: bool (the three as object.scale, for art that moves or scales with the artboard), lockedAndHidden?: bool (locked and hidden art moves along; default: the preference; recorded in the journal so a replay matches)} → null, or with scaleArt {scaled: the art scaled}; no undo step when nothing changes",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "artboard.switchOrientation",
   :label "Switch Orientation",
   :params
   "{index? | indices?, selectedArtboards?: [n…] (as artboard.duplicate), scaleArt?: bool (default: the Artboard tool's Scale Artwork with Artboard option), patterns?, lockedAndHidden?: bool (as artboard.setProps)} (default: the artboards the Artboard tool has selected, else its active one) each artboard swaps its width and height and keeps its top-left corner, in one undo step; a square artboard and a locked one stay as they are, the call fails with `the artboard is locked` when every artboard it names is locked, and when nothing else changes no undo step is recorded → {switched: [index…]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/panelcmds.rs"}
  {:id "assets.add",
   :label "Collect for Export",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selected objects; a layer id collects the art under it, including in its sublayers), multiple?: true (an asset per object; false: one asset of them all), name?: (the asset's name, when it makes one)} collect art as assets for Window › Asset Export and Export for Screens' Assets tab, named after the object (else Asset 1, Asset 2…); art already collected as such an asset keeps it → {assets: [asset id…] (in order), added: n}. Assets follow their art: moving it moves the crop, deleting it removes it from the asset",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "assets.add3D",
   :label "Export 3D Object",
   :params
   "{ids?: [id…] (default: the selected objects), format?: usda|usdz|gltf|obj (default usda)} collect each object with an Extrude & Bevel, Revolve, Inflate or Rotate effect as a 3D asset of Window › Asset Export, named after the object (else Asset 1, Asset 2…): assets.export3D writes it as a mesh file. An object already collected as a 3D asset keeps it; an object in ids without such an effect is refused. Without ids, the selected objects without one (on a group or layer, one on its fill or stroke draws nothing and does not count), and a selected object inside another selected object that has one, are left out; refused when none is left → {assets: [asset id…] (in order), added: n}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "assets.export",
   :label "Export Assets",
   :params
   "{assets?: [asset id…] (default all but the 3D assets, which assets.export3D writes), folder?, zip?, openLocation?, formats?, preset?, settings?, prefix?, subfolders?, antiAlias?} each asset's art alone, cropped to it, in every format row: document.exportForScreens {assets} at the document's export settings (document.exportSettings) under the ones given; with subfolders false every file goes into the folder itself, mobile and density rows too → what document.exportForScreens returns (no folder: the files, or one zip, as dataBase64; warnings name a key in the rows or settings given that only another format takes, not one in the remembered settings). Leaves the remembered settings as they are (assets.settings.set changes them)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "assets.export3D",
   :label "Export 3D Assets",
   :params
   "{assets?: [asset id…] (default every 3D asset), folder?, zip?} each 3D asset's object as a mesh file in its format (assets.set3DFormat), named after the asset: USDA or USDZ, glTF 2.0 (one .gltf, its buffer embedded) or OBJ with its .mtl (whitespace and # in an OBJ's name become _). Every solid of the object (the fill's, each stroke's, a group's members') is a mesh with a material in the color it is painted; faces turned away from the viewer are included, at the object's 3D rotation, y up, about the point it turns about, in points (glTF: meters). Files that would share a name get -2, -3…; an object with a hole that crosses its face's outline or another hole, or with more than 2,000,000 triangles, is refused → {files: [path…]} (no folder: {files: [{name, dataBase64}]}, or with zip one zip as {name, dataBase64, files})",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "assets.remove",
   :label "Remove Asset",
   :params
   "{assets: [asset id…]} take assets out of the Asset Export panel (their art stays) → {removed: n}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "assets.rename",
   :label "Rename Asset",
   :params "{asset: id, name} rename an asset (its files' names)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "assets.set3DFormat",
   :label "3D Export Format",
   :params
   "{assets: [asset id…], format: usda|usdz|gltf|obj} the mesh format 3D assets export to (Asset Export's Format for a 3D asset) → {changed: n}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "assets.settings.set",
   :label "Asset Export Settings",
   :params
   "{exportPreset?: (a preset of document.exportPresets.list: its formats or preset, its format settings over the saved ones, its prefix (none when it has none), its folders (or subfolders: rows or none) with subfolders on for rows, and antiAlias; the other keys go over it), formats?, preset?: mobile|density|\"\" (none), settings?, prefix?, subfolders?: true|false (Create Sub-folders: true sorts the files into a folder per row; false puts assets.export's files in the folder itself and, given without exportPreset, sets a remembered folder per format or item to none as well), antiAlias?, openLocation?: true|false (Open Location after Export: remembered in document.exportSettings, not in presets or the reply; given alone to a document without settings, Create Sub-folders stays on)} change the export settings the Asset Export panel and Export for Screens share (document.exportSettings; the values of document.exportForScreens; null removes one): formats replace a preset, a preset replaces the formats → {settings}. Not an undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/assets.rs"}
  {:id "attributes.set",
   :label "Attributes",
   :params
   "{overprintFill?: bool, overprintStroke?: bool (aimed as object.setOverprint's fill and stroke, item? too), showCenter?: bool (the canvas shows the selected object's centre point), imageMap?: \"none\"|\"rectangle\"|\"polygon\", url?: string (\"\" removes it; SVG, PDF and .ai export link the object), note?: string, ids?|id?, item?: appearance item index|null, target?: \"object\"|\"contents\"} set the Attributes panel's values on ids or the selection, as one undo step; a URL given joins the recent URLs (attributes.info) → {changed: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/attributes.rs"}
  {:id "brush.addFromLibrary",
   :label "Add to Brushes",
   :params
   "{library: id or name, name? | names?: [brush names in the library] (default: all of it), apply?: false (also apply the first one to paths, as brush.apply does), ids?|id? (the paths apply takes; default the selected ones), swatchConflict? (as edit.paste)} copy library brushes into the document's Brushes as one undo step (with the apply; named Apply Brush when no brush is added and it only applies one), with the resources their art uses (patterns, symbols, swatches, graphic styles, images). A brush the document already has (same name and definition) isn't added again; a name another brush has gets a number (\"Ribbon 2\"). The first one becomes the current brush → {library, names: [each brush's name in the document], added: [names added], existing: [names already there], applied: [ids of the paths it was applied to]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushlib.rs"}
  {:id "brush.apply",
   :label "Apply Brush",
   :params
   "{name, ids?|id?} apply a brush to the strokes of the selected paths (adds a stroke if missing) and make it current → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushsym.rs"}
  {:id "brush.delete",
   :label "Delete Brush",
   :params
   "{name} | {names: [name…]} delete brushes; strokes using them become plain strokes",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushsym.rs"}
  {:id "brush.duplicate",
   :label "Duplicate Brush",
   :params
   "{name, newName? (trimmed; blank: <name> copy)} | {names: [name…]} → {name} | {names}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushsym.rs"}
  {:id "brush.freehand",
   :label "Paintbrush",
   :params
   "{…params as path.freehand, brush?: name} paint a freehand stroke with a brush; without `brush` (or with null) the plain path is drawn; a `brush` that names no brush in the document, a `style` other than \"pencil\" or \"brush\", a `brush` for a path with no stroke (a continued or redrawn path without one, or a new filled \"pencil\" path while the stroke is None) and an unknown key are errors and nothing is drawn; the path and its brush are one undo step → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushsym.rs"}
  {:id "brush.loadLibrary",
   :label "Other Library…",
   :params
   "{path? | data?: file text | dataBase64?, name?: file name (default: the path's)} load the brushes of any document VectorCraft opens (see document.formats; one without brushes of its own has the default ones), a saved brush library included, for the library panel (Window → Brush Libraries lists it until the app quits; a file of the user library folder, or a file with the same bytes as one there, opens as that User Defined library) → {library: id, name, count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushlib.rs"}
  {:id "brush.move",
   :label "Move Brush",
   :params
   "{name? | names?: [brush names of one type, in order], to?: index among the brushes of that type in brush.list order (they go before the brush of that type now there that isn't moving; default: after the last one), type?: calligraphic|scatter|art|pattern|bristle (the type they go into; default: theirs)} reorder brushes within their type, as one undo step (none when the order stays as it was); brushes of different types, or a type that isn't theirs, are refused (brushes move only within their type) → {moved}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushsym.rs"}
  {:id "brush.new",
   :label "New Brush…",
   :params
   "{type: calligraphic|scatter|art|pattern|bristle, name? (trimmed; blank: New <Type> Brush; a bristle brush name, with the number a taken name gets, has at most 31 characters), params?: {…definition fields}, ids?|id?} new brush; art/scatter/pattern brushes take the selected art (pattern: side tile) unless params give it → {name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/brushsym.rs"}
  {:id "brush.options",
   :label "Brush Options…",
   :params
