rmat>, <scale>, <suffix> (else the row's suffix ends the name), YYYYMMDD, YYYY-MM-DD, YYYY, <date>, <time>, <YYYY>, <MM>, <DD>, <hh>, <mm> and <ss>; a trailing .ext is dropped, as in `COMPANY-Logo-<filename>-####-YYYYMMDD`; different files it names alike get -2, -3…), counterStart?: 1, counterPer?: item (every file of an item has its number)|file, date?: YYYY-MM-DD (the date the pattern uses; default today, UTC), preset?: mobile (PNG 1x, 2x, 3x) | density (PNG 0.75x–4x in ldpi…xxxhdpi sub-folders) instead of formats (turns subfolders on), formats?: [{format: png|png8|jpg|webp|gif|tiff|bmp|tga|psd|svg|svgz|pdf|eps|ai|vectorcraft, scale?: 1 | \"2x\" | \"100w\" | \"100h\" | \"72ppi\", width?: px | height?: px | ppi? (raster only; width, then height, then ppi win over scale), suffix?: (raster default: @2x, @100w, @100h, none at 1x; vector formats drop size suffixes), folder?: (its sub-folder), quality?: (jpg 0–100; webp 0–100 with lossless: false), …the format's options (antiAlias, background, preset (pdf)…)}], settings?: {png|png8|jpg|webp|gif|tiff|bmp|tga|psd|svg|svgz|pdf|eps|ai|vectorcraft: {…options for every row of that format}} (rows' own options win), prefix?, antiAlias?: none|art|type (raster rows without their own), openLocation?: (remembered; the app shows the files after exporting)} one file per artboard and format (a PDF holds its artboard alone; artboards with the same name, in any case, get -2, -3…; an unnamed one is Artboard-N; a row whose file would take a name another row's file has, in any case, gets -2, -3… too, and identical rows write one file; row folders that differ only in case are one folder, spelled as the first row spells it) → {files: [path…]} (into the folder of exportPreset, outside the automation read roots: no ZIP path, and files relative to that folder); no folder → {files: [{name, dataBase64}]} (names include sub-folders: 2x/Icon@2x.png); every reply has warnings: [the encoders' warnings for the files, each once: an image that couldn't be decoded, type written in the fallback font…]. eps, ai and vectorcraft rows write a document of the item alone (its one artboard). The params (but zip and assets) are remembered in the document (document.exportSettings; not an undo step). A key it doesn't take, a key no format takes in a format row or in settings, settings for a format it doesn't write, and an unknown key inside a PDF, EPS or SVG option's object, are refused; a key only another format takes in a row or in settings is not used, and warnings name it as given (formats[0].quality; a key in settings only when no row of that format reads it; not a key of an exportPreset). Under automation read roots, an svg or svgz row, and a row whose files carry the native document (vectorcraft, eps, ai but a version 7 file, a pdf with preserveEditing on that holds every artboard of the document it is written from), is refused, before the folder is made or any file is written, while the document links a JavaScript file outside them, or while the row's file would name a linked image's file outside them, as document.export refuses it",
