  {:id "document.setup",
   :label "Document Setup",
   :params
   "{units?: \"Points\"|\"Inches\"|\"Millimeters\"|…, bleed?: pt (all sides)|[top, bottom, left, right]|{top?, bottom?, left?, right?} (0–72 pt), outlineImages?: bool (show images in Outline mode), highlightSubstitutedGlyphs?: bool (Highlight Substituted Fonts is a preference: prefs.set highlightSubstitutedFonts; a highlightSubstitutedFonts key is ignored and the reply carries a warning),gridSize?: \"small\"|\"medium\"|\"large\", gridColors?: \"Light\"|\"Medium\"|\"Dark\"|\"Red\"|\"Orange\"|\"Green\"|\"Blue\"|\"Purple\"|[colour, colour] (transparency grid; the first is also the paper colour; #rrggbbaa and #rgba are refused), simulatePaper?: bool, flattenerPreset?: \"High Resolution\"|\"Medium Resolution\"|\"Low Resolution\"|a saved preset (flattener.presets.list), discardWhiteOverprint?: bool, language?: \"English: USA\"|\"German\"|\"French\"|… (also picks its quotes), quotes?: {double?: \"“”\", single?: \"‘’\"} (beside a language: only if they differ from the current ones), typographersQuotes?: bool (typed straight quotes become the document's quotes), superscript?: {size?: %, position?: %}, subscript?: {size?: %, position?: %}, smallCapsSize?: %, exportText?: \"editable\"|\"appearance\" (SVG text as text or as outlines), backgroundContents?: \"transparent\"|\"white\" (white: raster exports are white behind the art), alignNewObjectsToPixelGrid?: bool (Align New Objects to Pixel Grid: paths and compound paths drawn from then on are pixel-aligned, as object.setPixelAligned; art already in the document, pasted, duplicated or placed keeps its own setting), …the keys of its own reply (it can be passed back; the values it only reports are ignored)} change the document setup in one undo step; no params → the current setup",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/docsetup.rs"}
  {:id "document.switchUnits",
   :label "Switch Units",
   :params
   "{} the document's units become the next of Points, Picas, Inches, Millimeters, Centimeters, Pixels, Feet & Inches, Meters, Yards and Feet (the order a right-click on a ruler lists them), Feet going back to Points; one undo step → {units}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/edit.rs"}
  {:id "edit.assignProfile",
   :label "Assign Profile…",
   :params
   "{rgb?: profile|null, cmyk?: profile|null} tag the document with profiles (color numbers are kept; null: no profile, Don't Color Manage This Document, so colors show through the working space; the working space's name: that profile stays assigned when the working space changes). Colors then show and convert through the profiles assigned; the working spaces stay as edit.colorSettings set them → {rgb, cmyk}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colormgmt.rs"}
  {:id "edit.clear",
   :label "Clear",
   :params
   "{ids?, guides?: bool (with ids: also delete the selected ruler guides)} delete the objects `ids`, else the selection (fully selected objects and direct-selected anchors together, else ruler guides; a compound-path member selected on its own is deleted alone, and a compound left with no members goes too); without ids, refused while an object of a symbol instance's art is selected",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/edit.rs"}
  {:id "edit.clearHistory",
   :label "Clear History",
   :params
   "{} remove every undo and redo step of the active document (the History panel menu's Clear History): the document stays as it is, and clearing is not an undo step → {cleared: the number of steps removed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/edit.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colorSettings",
   :label "Color Settings…",
   :params
   "{rgb?: profile, cmyk?: profile, intent?: \"perceptual\"|\"relative\"|\"saturation\"|\"absolute\", bpc?: bool, rgbPolicy?: \"off\"|\"preserveEmbedded\"|\"convert\", cmykPolicy?: \"off\"|\"preserveEmbedded\"|\"convert\"|\"preserveNumbers\"} set the working spaces and the color management policies → {rgb, cmyk, intent, bpc, rgbPolicy, cmykPolicy, profiles: [{name, kind, builtin}]}. A policy decides what opening a document (document.open, file.newFromTemplate, file.revert) does with an RGB or CMYK profile it is tagged with that is not the working space: preserveEmbedded (default) keeps it; off and preserveNumbers take it off and keep the color numbers; convert converts the colors of that model into the working space with the intent and bpc and takes it off. The open reply's warnings name each profile taken off or converted, and a document a policy changed opens with unsaved changes. The desktop app and vectorcraft-cli keep them in `Color Settings.json` next to the preferences and use them again at the next start (not with VECTORCRAFT_NO_PREFS); saved settings naming a profile that is gone leave the defaults",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colormgmt.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.adjustBalance",
   :label "Adjust Color Balance…",
   :params
   "{mode?: \"rgb\"|\"cmyk\"|\"gray\"|\"global\" (default: from the channels given), r?, g?, b? | c?, m?, y?, k? | gray? | tint?: -100..100 (% added per channel, default 0; `tint` is global mode: it shifts the tints of colours and gradient stops linked to global and spot swatches, which stay linked, and leaves other colours and images alone), convert?: false (true: the results stay in the adjusted model; false: each colour keeps its own), fill?, stroke?, includeImages?, includePatterns?, ids?} reaching what edit.colors.invert does → {changed, notChanged, warning?} (as edit.colors.invert)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.blendFrontToBack",
   :label "Blend Front to Back",
   :params
   "{} ≥3 filled objects (solid fills or gradient meshes, which keep their shading): intermediate fills graded between the frontmost and backmost fill. On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the new fill, as for the other Blend commands (docs/mcp.md); no undo step when no fill changes → {changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.blendHorizontally",
   :label "Blend Horizontally",
   :params
   "{} ≥3 filled objects or meshes: fills graded between the leftmost and rightmost; no undo step when no fill changes → {changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.blendVertically",
   :label "Blend Vertically",
   :params
   "{} ≥3 filled objects or meshes: fills graded between the topmost and bottommost; no undo step when no fill changes → {changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.invert",
   :label "Invert Colors",
   :params
   "{fill?: true, stroke?: true, includeImages?: true, includePatterns?: true, ids?} replace each colour by its RGB inverse (keeps the colour model) in fills, strokes, text, gradient meshes (with fills), colorized image fills (their pixels stay unchanged), other embedded images (a recoloured copy) and pattern tiles (a new pattern swatch; the original stays), as one undo step (none when nothing changes). On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the new paint of the topmost visible fill and stroke, and on a graph label the new paint of its characters and rows for every label of its kind, and on a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring its rows for every line of its kind (docs/mcp.md) → {changed, notChanged: {locked, hidden} (when the selection is everything select.all takes: the locked and hidden objects it left out whose colors would have changed; an object both hidden and locked counts as hidden), warning?: set when notChanged counts any object}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.overprintBlack",
   :label "Overprint Black…",
   :params
   "{remove?: false, percentage?: 100, fill?: true, stroke?: true, includeCmyBlacks?: false, includeSpotBlacks?: false, ids?} make the black fills and/or strokes of the selection (or ids; groups: their contents; type: its characters) overprint, or stop (remove). Black: K ≥ percentage with no C, M or Y (any with includeCmyBlacks), not linked to a spot swatch (unless includeSpotBlacks); a gradient is black when every stop is → {changed: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colormgmt.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.saturate",
   :label "Saturate…",
   :params
   "{intensity: -100..100 (%; a number outside the range counts as its nearest end), fill?, stroke?, includeImages?, includePatterns?, ids?} scale saturation by (1 + intensity/100), reaching what edit.colors.invert does → {changed, notChanged, warning?} (as edit.colors.invert)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.toCMYK",
   :label "Convert to CMYK",
   :params
   "{fill?, stroke?, includeImages?, includePatterns?, ids?} (as edit.colors.invert) → {changed, notChanged, warning?}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.toGrayscale",
   :label "Convert to Grayscale",
   :params
   "{fill?, stroke?, includeImages?, includePatterns?, ids?} (as edit.colors.invert; an embedded image is stored with one gray channel) → {changed, notChanged, warning?}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.toIndexed",
   :label "Convert to Indexed Color…",
   :params
   "{reduction?: \"selective\" (default)|\"perceptual\"|\"adaptive\"|\"web\"|\"gray\"|\"blackWhite\" (chosen as for a PNG-8 export)|\"uniform\" (evenly spaced levels of red, green and blue: the most levels, 2 to 6, whose cube fits in `colors` with one entry left for transparency)|\"document\" (the colors of the document's swatches, at most 255), colors?: 2..256 (default 256; the most palette entries, the transparent one included; at least 9 for uniform; refused for blackWhite and document), dither?: \"diffusion\" (default)|\"pattern\"|\"noise\"|\"none\", ditherAmount?: 0..100 (default 100), ids?} store each embedded image in the selection (in groups too) as an indexed-color PNG: a palette of at most 256 RGB colors, each pixel the index of one; pixels under half opacity become one transparent entry and the others opaque, keeping their color; linked images, colorized images and the images of color glyphs in outlined type keep their pixels; each image changed becomes a new image, one undo step for all; an image that is an indexed PNG already and would show the same pixels is left as it is, and no undo step is recorded when no image changes; an image of more than 134,217,728 pixels (33,554,432 in the web app) is refused with an error and nothing changes; reduction and dither ids are read as for a PNG-8 export, ignoring case → {changed: images changed, notChanged: the locked and hidden objects Select All left out that hold an image that is not an indexed PNG yet, warning?} (as edit.colors.invert)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.colors.toRGB",
   :label "Convert to RGB",
   :params
   "{fill?, stroke?, includeImages?, includePatterns?, ids?} (as edit.colors.invert) → {changed, notChanged, warning?}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/colorcmds.rs"}
  {:id "edit.copy",
   :label "Copy",
   :params
   "{selectedArtboards?: [n…] (the artboards the Artboard tool had selected, which the journal records for a replay; it runs artboard.copy with any tool chosen), art?: bool (default: the Artboard tool's moveArt option; the journal records it beside selectedArtboards), lockedAndHidden?: bool (the Artboard tool chosen, as artboard.copy)} the selection with what it uses (a compound-path member selected on its own, whole or in part, with Direct or Group Selection, is copied as an ordinary path with the compound's paint, transparency, opacity mask, fill rule and graphic style link (while it has that style's look), a gradient keeping the compound's fit; the compound is copied when it is selected, or when every member is selected whole outside isolation mode), and the selected ruler guides (pasted on the layer new art goes to, moved as the objects are; alone, where they were); the Artboard tool chosen: artboard.copy; with an object of a symbol instance's art selected, the instance is copied whole → {copied, guides}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/edit.rs"}
  {:id "edit.cut",
   :label "Cut",
