  {:id "file.saveAsTemplate",
   :label "Save as Template…",
   :params
   "{…as document.save} {path? (saved with the format's extension: one naming another format is replaced, and one is added to a name without it), format?: template (default) | ait (also when format is not given and the path ends in .ait), compress?, version?, preview?, precision?} a template that opens as a new untitled document: a native template (.vctemplate), or a PDF-compatible .ait written as a .ai file is (the .ai options and the PDF options, as document.save takes them for .ai; aiVersion 7 is an error); the document is unchanged → {path, format, bytes, warnings}; no path → {dataBase64, format, name: \"<name> template.<ext>\", folder: the Templates folder (preference templatesFolder), warnings}. Under automation read roots, it is refused, before any file is written, while the document links a JavaScript file outside them, as document.save refuses it",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/save.rs"}
  {:id "file.saveCopy",
   :label "Save a Copy…",
   :params
   "{…as document.save} {path?, format?, options?, precision?} write a copy; the document keeps its path, title and modified state → {path, format, bytes, warnings}; no path → {dataBase64, format, name: \"<name> copy.<ext>\", folder?, warnings}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/save.rs"}
  {:id "gradient.presets.apply",
   :label "Apply Gradient Preset",
   :params
   "{name: a preset's name (gradient.presets.list), stroke?, item?, ids?|id?, target? (as paint.editGradient)} give the gradient behind the active proxy (or the targeted fill or stroke) the preset's type, stops, method, spread and repeats (a freeform preset's: the first three), and a fill its dither, keeping its placement; a solid or no paint becomes the gradient. One undo step, as paint.editGradient → {name, ids: the objects painted (none: only the default changed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/gradpresets.rs"}
  {:id "gradient.selectStop",
   :label "Select Gradient Stop",
   :params
   "{index: stop index (0 = the start) | null to clear} select a stop of the gradient behind the active proxy (the first selected object's, else the default paint): the stop the Gradient tool's annotator, the Gradient and Color panels and Delete/arrow keys act on; refused while an object of a symbol instance's art is selected → {index}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/gradient.rs"}
  {:id "graph.column",
   :label "Column…",
   :params
   "{id?, seriesIndexes?: [index], design?: name|null, columnType?: vertical|uniform|repeating|sliding, each?: value (more than 0), fractions?: chop|scale} draw the columns or bars and the legend swatch of the series selected with Group Selection (or listed, or every series) with a graph design, its backmost object as its frame and its guides left out: vertical stretches it along the value axis to each column's length at the column's width, uniform scales it both ways to that length, centered on the column, repeating stacks copies out from the zero line that each stand for `each` and cuts off the last one where the value ends (chop) or scales it down to fit (scale) (vertical when one copy would be longer than the canvas), and sliding scales the part above its horizontal guide line (in bar graphs, right of a vertical one) in proportion to the column's width and stretches the part below to fill the rest (vertical without a guide, or in a column too short for the part above); type in the design that holds a `%` followed by two digits shows each column's value in place of the `%` and the digits, the first digit giving the least number of places before the decimal point (zeros added in front; 0 = as many as the value needs) and the second digit giving the places after it (rounded half away from zero), at the type's own size where the design's copy puts it (a repeating design shows it once, where a whole copy ending at the value end puts it; type inside a group that clips, is hidden or has its own opacity, blend mode, isolation, knockout, appearance or opacity mask, or inside a blend, compound shape, envelope, repeat or intertwine, stays there and is filled in each copy, drawn with the design; type inside a symbol stays as typed), and is left out of the legend swatch (a design of such type alone gets the default swatch); the design keeps its own orientation for negative values, and columns drawn with a design cast no drop shadow; null = plain columns; options left out keep the series' shared ones, else vertical, 10 and chop. Column, stacked column, bar and stacked bar series. No design → {designs: [names], design: the selected series' design or null, columnType, each, fractions}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "graph.create",
   :label "Create Graph",
   :params
   "{type: column|stackedColumn|bar|stackedBar|line|area|scatter|pie|radar, x, y, width, height, series?: [..], categories?: [..], rows?: [[number|null]], csv?} → {id}; an empty CSV cell or a null is a blank value, a number in straight quotes is a label; a `type` that is not a string, a `width` or `height` that is not a number, and data of the wrong type (as `graph.setData` reads it) are refused",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "graph.design",
   :label "Design…",
   :params
   "{new?: name|true (New Design: the selected art becomes a graph design, named \"New Design\" when true; put a rectangle at the back to set the size it draws at), rename?: name, to?: new name (the graphs drawing it follow), paste?: name (Paste Design: a copy of the design's art into the document, selected, to edit and save again), delete?: name|[names] (graphs drawing them go back to their default marks), ids?|id?: object ids (default: the selection), selectUnused?: bool (Select Unused: just the list)}; no params or selectUnused → {designs: [names], unused: [the names no graph draws with]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "graph.marker",
   :label "Marker…",
   :params
   "{id?, seriesIndexes?: [index], design?: name|null} draw the data points and legend swatch of the series selected with Group Selection (or listed, or every series) with a graph design, scaled so its backmost object fills the default marker's square; null = the default marker. Line, scatter and radar series. No design → {designs: [names], design: the selected series' design or null}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "graph.setData",
   :label "Data…",
   :params
   "{id?, series?, categories?, rows?, csv?: first row = series labels (first cell empty); then one row per category: label; values…; an empty cell or a null is a blank value; a quoted number a label; a `|` in a label a line break, transpose?: true swaps rows and columns (Transpose row/column), switchXY?: true swaps each scatter series' y and x columns (Switch x/y)} replace the graph's data; a `csv` that is not a string, `series` or `categories` that are not lists, `rows` that are not lists of numbers and nulls, or a `transpose` or `switchXY` that is not true or false is refused and the graph stays as it was; no data → the current {csv, series, categories, rows}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "graph.setType",
   :label "Type…",
   :params
   "{id?, type?, seriesIndexes?: [index], columnWidth?: % (1–1000; past 100 columns overlap), clusterWidth?: % (1–1000), legend?: bool, markPoints?: bool, connectPoints?: bool, edgeToEdge?: bool (line graphs: true runs the lines across the whole plot, false puts the points at the centres of their categories), ticks?: n, axisMin?: number|null (null = calculated), axisMax?: number|null, valueAxis?: left|right|both (the bar graphs' value axis stays along the bottom), separateScales?: bool, rightTicks?: n, rightAxisMin?, rightAxisMax?, tickLength?: none|short|full, tickMarks?: n per division, rightTickLength?, rightTickMarks?, categoryTickLength?: none|short|full, categoryTickMarks?: n, ticksBetweenLabels?: bool, prefix?, suffix?, rightPrefix?, rightSuffix?: text around the value axis numbers, firstRowInFront?: bool, firstColumnInFront?: bool (which overlapping columns are drawn on top: the first category over the next within each series, the first series over the others), filledLines?: bool (Draw Filled Lines: connecting lines as bands `lineWidth` wide filled with the series colour), lineWidth?: pt (Line Width of Draw Filled Lines: 0.01–1000; 3), dropShadow?: bool (Add Drop Shadow: a translucent black shadow down and right of the columns, bars, lines and pie wedges), legendAcrossTop?: bool (Add Legend Across Top: the legend in rows above the plot), pieLegend?: none|standard|wedges (Legends in Wedges: the series labels inside their wedges), piePosition?: ratio|even|stacked (several pies sized by their totals, at one size (the default), or stacked), pieSort?: all|first|none (wedges largest first in each pie, in the first pie's order, or in data order (the default)); the query lists the pie options for pie graphs} change the graph type and options; with `seriesIndexes`, or (no `id`) with only series selected with Group Selection, `type` goes to those series only and `valueAxis` (left|right; both is refused) puts them on that value axis, while the other options still apply to the whole graph (Combine different graph types: column, stacked column, line and area mix, and so do bar and stacked bar; a series given the graph's type follows the graph again) (axisMin and axisMax together override the calculated value axis: exactly that range in `ticks` divisions, 5 when 0; with the value axis on both sides, separateScales gives the series on the right axis a scale of their own, set the same way with rightTicks, rightAxisMin and rightAxisMax); a value of the wrong type, such as \"10\" for a number or \"true\" for a bool, or a negative count, is refused and the graph stays as it was; options that leave the graph as it is record no step of history; a null is read as a key left out, except that a null axis bound goes back to the calculated value; no options → the current ones",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.addFromLibrary",
   :label "Add to Graphic Styles",
   :params
   "{library: id or name, name? | names?: [style names in the library] (default: all of it), apply?: false (also apply the first one to `ids` or the selection, if any, as graphicStyle.apply), add?: false (with apply: add its appearance on top, as Alt-click), ids?} copy library styles into the document's Graphic Styles as one undo step (with the apply). A style the document already has (same name and look) isn't added again; a name taken by another style gets a number (\"Halo 2\"). The patterns they paint with come along (a name taken by another pattern or swatch gets a number) → {library, added: [names in the document], existing: [names already there], applied?: name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stylelib.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.apply",
   :label "Apply Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{name, add?: bool, ids?|id? (layers too), target?: \"object\"|\"contents\"} give the objects (default: the selection; a group or layer itself, its fills and strokes painting its members and its effects applying to them as one piece; target contents: the objects inside instead) the style's appearance, opacity, blend mode, isolate and knockout, and link them to it (placed gradients land at the same place relative to each object's bounds); add: true (Alt-click) adds its fills, strokes and effects on top of the existing appearance instead and unlinks. On a path directly in a graph series (a series group's id stands for those paths), the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke (with `add`: of the kinds of row the style shows) and, without `add`, the object's opacity and blend mode (exceptions, and the art of a graph design in a series, which is left out: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows (with `add`: of the kinds of row the style shows) and, without `add`, its object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind. With nothing selected (and no ids) the next object drawn takes the style instead (see appearance.newArt) → {newArt: true}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.breakLink",
   :label "Break Link to Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, target?: \"object\"|\"contents\"} unlink the objects (default: the selection) from their graphic style; they keep their look. A graph series group's id stands for the group and the paths directly in it, a graph's Axes group for the group and its lines and labels, and its Legend group for the group and its labels",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.delete",
   :label "Delete Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{name} | {names: [name…]} delete styles; their objects keep their look but are unlinked",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.duplicate",
   :label "Duplicate Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{name} a copy of the style at the end of the list, named `<name> copy` (`<name> copy 2`… when that is taken); no object is linked to it → {name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.loadLibrary",
   :label "Other Library…",
   :params
   "{path? | data?: file text | dataBase64?, name?: file name (default: the path's)} load a .vcstyles library, or the graphic styles of any document VectorCraft opens (see document.formats), for the library panel (Window → Graphic Style Libraries lists it until the app quits; a file of the user library folder, or a file with the same extension and bytes as one there, opens as that User Defined library; a .ai or EPS style painting with one of the file's gradients by name takes it at the style's angle, fitted to each object it is applied to, VectorCraft's own placement) → {library: id, name, count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stylelib.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.merge",
   :label "Merge Graphic Styles",
   :params
   "{names: [name…] (two or more), name?} add a style combining the styles' fills, strokes and effects (each style's on top of the ones before it) with the first one's opacity, blend mode, isolate and knockout → {name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.move",
   :label "Move Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{name, to: index} move the style to position `to` of the list (0 = first, clamped), as dragging it in the Graphic Styles panel does",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.new",
   :label "New Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{name?, id?} a style from object `id` or the first selected object: its appearance, opacity, blend mode, isolate and knockout (a group without fills or strokes of its own lends its topmost object's, type its characters'; a graph series group with no fill, stroke, effect, opacity, blend mode, isolation, knockout or style link of its own stands for the topmost path directly in it, and a graph's Axes or Legend group with none of these for its topmost line or label; placed gradients are kept relative to its bounds); links the object, unless it is the art of a graph design in a series. Names are made unique → {name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.redefine",
   :label "Redefine Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{name?, id?} replace the style (default: the one the object was last linked to) with the look of object `id` or the first selected object (a graph series group with no fill, stroke, effect, opacity, blend mode, isolation, knockout or style link of its own: the topmost path directly in it; a graph's Axes or Legend group: its topmost line or label); the objects still linked to it update, and that object becomes linked. The art of a graph design in a series keeps its look and is unlinked, as the source or as a linked object. A linked graph series group passes the style to the paths directly in it, a linked Axes group to its lines and labels and a linked Legend group to its labels, other than the source and paths linked to the style whose look was edited, and is left cleared (as appearance.clear) and unlinked. On a linked path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of the topmost visible fill and stroke and the object's opacity and blend mode (exceptions: docs/mcp.md); on a graph label, or a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring (a graph's Axes group stands for the lines and labels directly in it, its Legend group for the labels), the graph stores that object's topmost visible fill and stroke rows and object opacity and blend mode for every label or line of its kind → {name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.rename",
   :label "Rename Graphic Style",
   :params
   "{name, to} (Graphic Style Options; names are unique and linked objects stay linked) → {name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.saveLibrary",
   :label "Save Graphic Style Library…",
   :params
   "{path?, names?: [style names] (default: all), name?: library name (default: the document's), user?: false (save into the user library folder, listed under User Defined)} save the document's graphic styles as a .vcstyles library (JSON: the styles, unlinked from swatches, and the patterns they paint with) → {path, count, library?: id when saved to the user folder}; without path or user → {data: the file's text, count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stylelib.rs"}
  {:id "graphicStyle.sortByName",
   :label "Sort by Name",
   :params
   "{} sort the styles by name (the Default Graphic Style stays first)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/style.rs"}
  {:id "guide.add",
   :label "Add Guide",
   :params
   "{vertical: bool, pos: pt (x for vertical, y for horizontal), artboard?: index (0-based whole number; an artboard guide: it runs across that artboard only and moves, is copied and is deleted with it; default, or null, a canvas guide, across the whole canvas), layer?: id (the layer it is on, shown, hidden, locked and deleted with it; default the current layer)} → {index}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/docmenu.rs"}
  {:id "guide.move",
   :label "Move Guide",
   :params
   "{index, pos: pt} | {dx?, dy?: pt, copy?: bool} put ruler guide `index` at `pos`, or move the selected guides (vertical ones by dx, horizontal ones by dy); copy leaves them and selects the moved copies",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/docmenu.rs"}
  {:id "guide.remove",
   :label "Remove Guide",
   :params
   "{index?, indexes?: [index…] (at most 10,000)} delete ruler guide `index` (or guides `indexes`, as dragging their rows onto the Layers panel's trash does), else the selected ones (as Delete / edit.clear does), in one undo step; give `index` or `indexes`, not both, and an index given twice counts once; a hidden or locked guide, or one on a hidden or locked layer, is an error → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/docmenu.rs"}
  {:id "guide.select",
   :label "Select Guides",
   :params
   "{indexes: [index…] (at most 10,000), toggle?: bool} select ruler guides on their own (deselecting the art); toggle adds or removes them instead, keeping the selected art (a Shift-click on a guide) → {selected: [index…]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/docmenu.rs"}
  {:id "guide.setLayer",
   :label "Move Guide to Layer",
   :params
   "{index?, indexes?: [index…] (at most 10,000), layer: id} put ruler guide `index` (or guides `indexes`), else the selected guides, on layer `layer` (a layer or sublayer), as dragging their rows onto that layer's row in the Layers panel does; give `index` or `indexes`, not both, and an index given twice counts once → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/docmenu.rs"}
  {:id "imageTrace.expand",
   :label "Expand",
   :params
   "{id?, ids?: [id…] (instead of id), byColor?: false (each color's paths in a group of their own, named by the swatch the color links to or as #rrggbb, gradient fills in one group named Gradients; the groups stack by their lowest path and keep their paths' order; a color whose paths overlap another color's from above and below gets a group for each part, so the art draws the same; refused for a trace made with autoGrouping and for a trace with a live Pathfinder effect)} keep only the traced paths (drop the source image) → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "imageTrace.make",
   :label "Make",
   :params
   "{id?: image or Image Trace group (default: selection), preset?: name (imageTrace.presets), savedPreset?: {settings} (a saved preset's settings, which the journal records so a replay traces with them after the preset is changed, renamed or deleted; used in place of the saved preset `preset` names), enhanced?: false (the preset's enhanced version: with Auto Grouping, and with Shapes in all but High Fidelity Photo; Flat Logo has none and is traced as it is), params?: {mode: \"blackAndWhite\"|\"grayscale\"|\"color\"|\"logo\", threshold: 0-255, palette: \"limited\"|\"fullTone\"|\"automatic\"|\"documentLibrary\" (color mode; limited: the `colors` best colours, fullTone: as many as the tones need, more with colorDetail, automatic: flat art with its own colours, else fullTone, documentLibrary: at most `colors` of the library's colours, as they are), colors: 2-256, colorDetail: 0-100 (fullTone, automatic), library: \"document\" (the document's swatches) or a swatch library id or name (swatch.library.list; documentLibrary), colorGroup?: name (color mode, documentLibrary with library \"document\": the colors of that document color group instead of every swatch; \"\" is every swatch), paths: 0-100, corners: 0-100, noise: px (an area smaller than this joins the color it shares the longest border with; when that color is far from its own and the area is 2 px or more, or a single pixel whose longest border is not tied between colors, it joins the neighboring color nearest its pixels among those sharing at least a tenth of that border), method: \"abutting\"|\"overlapping\" (abutting with fills, not mode logo: a \"Seam Fills\" clip group under the paths holds strokes along the edges two filled paths share, 1.5 image pixels wide (VectorCraft's own width), in the color of the lower path (on an image stretched more one way than another, each stroke's outline in image pixels as a filled path), clipped to the image's box within the traced paths' box; paths that became live shapes get none; the paths are not changed), ignoreWhite (leave out white areas), ignoreColor?: \"#rrggbb\" (with ignoreWhite: the colour left out instead of white), ignoreBackground: false (with ignoreWhite: only the areas of the ignored color that reach the image's edge are left out), keepColors?: [\"#rrggbb\"…] (not mode logo: only the palette colors within about 30 levels of a listed color are traced; empty: every color), snapCurvesToLines, shapes: false (filled outlines that are a circle, an ellipse, a rectangle or a regular polygon come out as that live shape), autoGrouping: false (each path that has others inside it is grouped with them), gradients: false (grayscale and color: an area whose colour changes evenly along one direction is one path with a linear gradient fill), fills: true, strokes: false (Create: lines up to strokeWidth wide become stroked centre lines; without fills, wider areas become stroked outlines), strokeWidth: px (10), logoColors?: [\"#rrggbb\"…] (mode logo: flat-colour logos only; colours found automatically or named here, at most ten; white is its own color, and a named color with every channel 245 or more is taken as that white, except with logoColors named, logoWhite false and no ignoreWhite; noise = areas under noise/10 px ignored; edges to a fraction of a pixel, sharp corners restored, lines and circles snapped; enclosed transparent areas are painted white while white is its own color, and stay holes with ignoreWhite or without a white of its own; fills/strokes are ignored; gradients and photos are refused, judged by the image's own colors also when logoColors are named), logoWhite: true (mode logo with logoColors named; false traces the named colors only: white areas take the nearest of them, a named white is kept and enclosed transparent areas stay holes; with ignoreWhite, white areas are left out either way)}, view?: as imageTrace.setView (default: the traced object's own, else tracingResult), ids?: [id…] (instead of id)} → {id, paths, anchors, colors, warnings: [text…] (the image is over 1500 px on a side, so it traces more slowly; or it was traced scaled down; Flat Logo names only the size it traced a larger image at; or a keepColors color matches none the trace found, or nothing was traced)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "imageTrace.makeAndExpand",
   :label "Make and Expand",
   :params
   "{…as imageTrace.make, byColor?: false (each color's paths in a group of their own, as imageTrace.expand)} same as imageTrace.make, then expand → {id, paths, anchors, colors, warnings: [text…] (as imageTrace.make)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "imageTrace.release",
   :label "Release",
   :params
   "{id?, ids?: [id…] (instead of id)} put the source image back in place of Image Trace groups → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "imageTrace.setView",
   :label "Image Trace View",
   :params
   "{id?|ids?: Image Trace objects (default: selection), view: \"tracingResult\"|\"tracingResultWithOutlines\"|\"outlines\"|\"outlinesWithSourceImage\"|\"sourceImage\"} how they draw on screen; exports, printing and Expand keep the tracing result → {ids, view}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "layer.clippingMask.toggle",
   :label "Make/Release Clipping Mask",
   :params
   "{id?: layer or group (default: the one highlighted layer or group row, else the one selected group, else the current layer)} make: its top object (a path, compound path or text, which loses its paint) clips the rest and moves to the bottom (new art added on top is clipped); release: it stops clipping, the clipping path stays unpainted → {clip}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.collectInNew",
   :label "Collect in New Layer",
   :params
   "{ids?} move rows (default: the highlighted rows, else the selected objects) into a new layer where the topmost of them was (a sublayer when they are in a layer), deselecting every selected object left hidden or locked (the key object too) → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.delete",
   :label "Delete Selection",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} delete rows: layers, sublayers, groups or objects with what they hold (default: the highlighted rows, else the current layer). The last layer stays → {deleted}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.duplicate",
   :label "Duplicate Selection",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} copy rows (default: the highlighted rows, else the current layer), each just above its original; a layer's copy is named `<name> copy`. The copies are highlighted → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.flatten",
   :label "Flatten Artwork",
   :params
   "{id?} (default: the highlighted row's top-level layer, else the current one's) move the art of every other visible top-level layer into this one, keeping the stacking order; hidden layers and their art are deleted, template layers stay. Every selected object left hidden or locked, such as one flattened into a locked layer, is deselected (the key object too). One undo step → {id, discarded}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.hideOthers",
   :label "Hide Others",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} hide every top-level layer but those holding the highlighted rows (else the current layer), which show. One undo step → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.highlight",
   :label "Highlight Rows",
   :params
   "{ids, mode?: \"set\"|\"add\"|\"toggle\"} highlight Layers panel rows (Shift-click: a range, Ctrl-click: toggle one); the last one's layer becomes current. Not an undo step → {rows}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.locate",
   :label "Locate Object",
   :params
   "{id?} (default: the last selected object) highlight the object's row; the Layers panel opens the layers around it and scrolls to it → {id, ancestry: [layer…, id]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.lockOthers",
   :label "Lock Others",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} lock every top-level layer but those holding the highlighted rows (else the current layer), which unlock → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.merge",
   :label "Merge Selected",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} (default: the highlighted rows) merge two or more rows into the layer listed (highlighted) last: the other layers' contents and the other rows move into it, keeping their stacking order, and the emptied layers go. Every selected object left hidden or locked, such as one merged into a hidden or locked layer, is deselected (the key object too). One undo step → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.move",
   :label "Move Rows",
   :params
   "{ids|id, target, place?: \"above\"|\"below\"|\"inside\" (default inside), copy?: bool} drag rows in the Layers panel: above or below the target row (beside it, in its layer or group), or inside a layer, group or Intertwine group (on top of its contents). Layers go only in layers or at the top level, objects in layers, groups and Intertwine groups; an object placed beside a top-level layer goes inside it. An object placed in an Intertwine group becomes a member drawn in its row's order, with no arranged areas, and one placed in a group that is a member becomes part of that member; one that is or holds an Intertwine group, a Repeat, a graph or a Live Paint group is refused. A member moved out of its Intertwine group drops its arranged areas, and a group left with one member is replaced by that member, or becomes a plain group of it when the group has an opacity, blending, appearance, mask, lock or hidden state of its own (with no member, it is removed). A row never goes into itself; a locked layer or group takes nothing. `copy` (Alt-drag) moves copies. Every selected object left hidden or locked, such as one moved into a hidden layer or group, is deselected (the key object too). One undo step → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.new",
   :label "New Layer…",
   :params
   "{name?, top?: bool, below?: bool, color?, template?, locked?, visible?, printable?, preview?, dimImages?} a layer directly above the current layer, at its level (a sublayer beside a current sublayer); `top`: above all layers (Ctrl/Cmd-click the button); `below`: directly below the current layer, at its level (Ctrl/Cmd+Alt-click the button), not with `top`. Options as layer.setProps; refused while an opacity mask is edited (the Layers panel lists only the mask) → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.newSublayer",
   :label "New Sublayer…",
   :params
   "{parent?: layer id (default: the highlighted row's layer, else the current layer), bottom?: bool, name?, …options as layer.new} a sublayer on top of the parent's contents; `bottom`: under the parent's contents, above a clipping layer's clipping path (Ctrl/Cmd+Alt-click the button); refused while an opacity mask is edited → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.outlineOthers",
   :label "Outline Others",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} turn Preview off (outline view) for every top-level layer but those holding the highlighted rows (else the current layer), which preview → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.pasteRemembersLayers",
   :label "Paste Remembers Layers",
   :params
   "{on?} (default: toggle) the document option: on, the Paste commands put objects back into the layers or sublayers they were copied from (in that document while they are still there, else by the names of the layer and the layers around it, the topmost match first; a missing sublayer is made inside its layer, a missing top-level layer on top; a hidden or locked one is an error and nothing is pasted), off into the current layer; one undo step when it changes (document.inspect → pasteRemembersLayers) → {on}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.previewAll",
   :label "Preview All Layers",
   :params "{} turn Preview on for every layer and sublayer → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.releaseToLayers",
   :label "Release to Layers (Sequence)",
   :params
   "{id?: layer or group (default: the highlighted row, else the current layer), build?: bool} each object in it goes into a new sublayer of its own, in stacking order (a group's objects go into sublayers of its layer, where the group was). `build`: Release to Layers (Build), each new sublayer holds copies of the objects up to its own, so the layers add up. One undo step → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.releaseToLayersBuild",
   :label "Release to Layers (Build)",
   :params "{id?} layer.releaseToLayers with build: true → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.reverse",
   :label "Reverse Order",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} (default: the highlighted rows) reverse the stacking order of two or more rows that share a layer or group; each keeps the places the others held. One undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.selectAll",
   :label "Select Art",
   :params
   "{id, add?: bool} the Layers panel's selection column: select the visible, unlocked art of a layer (its sublayers' too), or the object itself; `add` (Shift-click) adds it to the selection, or removes it when it is all selected already → {selected: [..]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.setCurrent",
   :label "Set Current Layer",
   :params
   "{id} click a row: it alone is highlighted, and the layer it is (or the layer it is in) becomes the current layer, where new art goes. Not an undo step → {id, layer}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.setProps",
   :label "Layer Options…",
   :params
   "{ids?|id? (default: the highlighted rows, else the current layer), name? (with prefs.identifyObjectsBy xmlId: a valid XML ID, stored as the object name), visible?, locked?, template?, printable?, preview?, dimImages?: 0..100|false, color?: index 0..26|\"#rrggbb\"|preset name (a hex color with an alpha part, #rrggbbaa or #rgba, is an error)} Layer Options; rows that are not layers take name, visible and locked, and `ids` may name ruler guides (their `guide.list` id), which hide or lock on their own. Template on also locks the layer and dims its images to 50% (unless given); off unlocks it and stops dimming. One undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.showAll",
   :label "Show All Layers",
   :params "{} show every layer and sublayer → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.target",
   :label "Target",
   :params
   "{id, add?: bool (Shift-click: the item joins the selection, or leaves it when all selected; nothing is targeted)} target a layer, group or object as clicking its target circle in the Layers panel does: a layer gets its visible, unlocked art (its sublayers' too) selected and becomes the current layer, and appearance.*, effect.*, transparency.* and the opacity-mask commands without `ids` then act on the layer itself; anything else is selected. Any other selection change ends the targeting (`document.inspect` → target) → {id, selected: [..]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "layer.template",
   :label "Template",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, on?: bool (default: toggle the first)} make layers templates (locked, dimmed, left out of print and export) or ordinary layers again (layer.setProps template) → {on}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "layer.unlockAll",
   :label "Unlock All Layers",
   :params "{} unlock every layer and sublayer → {count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layerpanel.rs"}
  {:id "library.add",
   :label "Add to Library",
   :params
   "{library?: id or name (default: the current library, made when there is none), kind: graphic|fillColor|strokeColor|fillGradient|strokeGradient|fillPattern|strokePattern|charStyle|paraStyle, ids?: objects (default: the selection), name?, color?: colour (a colour to add, instead of the selection's; #rrggbbaa and #rgba are refused), swatch?: a gradient or pattern swatch of the document (fillGradient…strokePattern: added instead of the selection's paint; with `color`, the spot swatch it is, kept as a spot colour), tint?: 0..100 (with `color` and a spot `swatch`: its %), group?: name, before?: item | after?: item (an item of the same kind)} add an item from the selection: graphic: a copy of the objects with every resource they use; fillColor/strokeColor: the first selected object's solid fill/stroke colour (else the default fill/stroke), a colour linked to a spot swatch kept as a spot colour (the swatch's name, its colour and the tint); fillGradient/strokeGradient: the first selected object's fill/stroke gradient (else the default's), without its placement or swatch links, named after its swatch, else \"Gradient\"; fillPattern/strokePattern: the first selected object's fill/stroke pattern (else the default's) with the resources its art uses, named after it; charStyle/paraStyle: the selected text's character/paragraph attributes (the Type tool's range, else the first selected text object). A new item goes into `group` (default: none) and, with `before` or `after`, just before or after that item in the order its kind is shown in, as dropping it among the Libraries panel's items does; an item the library already has (same kind and contents) isn't added again, nor moved → {library, kind, name, id?: graphic id, existing: bool, group?: name or null (a new item's)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.addToCharacterStyles",
   :label "Add to Character Styles",
   :params
   "{library?, item: a character style's name, recorded?: the style as it was when added (recorded in the journal so a replay matches)} add a library character style to the document's character styles without applying it (no text needs to be selected): a document style of that name with the same attributes is reused, a name taken by different attributes gets a number; a color linked to a swatch that isn't a global or spot swatch of the document keeps the color it shows, unlinked; a new style is one undo step, a reused one none → {style: its name in the document, existing: bool}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.create",
   :label "Create New Library",
   :params
   "{name?: \"My Library\"} a new empty library (its file in the library folder), made the current one → {id, name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.createGroup",
   :label "New Library Group",
   :params
   "{library?, name?: \"Group\" (a name the library's groups have, ignoring case, gets a number), items?: [{kind, item}] (moved into it out of their groups)} a new group of items, after the others → {library, group: its name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.delete",
   :label "Delete Library",
   :params
   "{library?} delete a library (default: the current one) and its file; not undoable → null",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.deleteGroup",
   :label "Delete Library Group",
   :params
   "{library?, group: name} delete a group: its items stay in the library, ungrouped → {library, ungrouped: how many}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.moveGroup",
   :label "Move Library Group",
   :params
   "{library?, group: name, to: index} move a group to position `to` of the library's groups (0 = first; past the end: last), as dragging its header in the Libraries panel does → {library, group, to: where it went}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.moveItem",
   :label "Move Library Item to Group",
   :params
   "{library?, kind, item: name (graphic: id or name), group?: name (null or none: out of its group), before?: item | after?: item (an item of the same kind, named as `item` is)} put an item in a group (out of the one it was in); with `before` or `after`, also move it just before or after that item in the order its kind is shown in, as dragging it in the Libraries panel does → {library, kind, item, group: name or null}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.removeItem",
   :label "Delete Library Item",
   :params
   "{library?, kind, item: name (graphic: id or name)} delete an item (out of its group too) → null",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.rename",
   :label "Rename Library",
   :params
   "{library?, name} rename a library (default: the current one) → {id, name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.renameGroup",
   :label "Rename Library Group",
   :params
   "{library?, group: name, name} rename a group (another group's name, ignoring case, is an error) → {library, group: the new name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.renameItem",
   :label "Rename Library Item",
   :params
   "{library?, kind, item: name (graphic: id or name), name: string (trimmed; 1 to 256 characters)} rename an item; it keeps its place and its group; another item of its kind with that name is an error, and its own name changes nothing; not undoable → {library, kind, item: its key now (graphic: its id), name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.setCurrent",
   :label "Show Library",
   :params
   "{library: id or name} the library the Libraries panel shows, which library commands without a `library` act on → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "library.use",
   :label "Use Library Item",
   :params
   "{library?, kind, item: name (graphic: id or name), center?: [x, y] (graphic; default: the first artboard's centre), to?: fill|stroke (colors, gradients, patterns; default: the kind's), recorded?: the item as it was when used (recorded in the journal so a replay matches)} graphic: place a copy centred on `center`, its resources pasted along, selected, one undo step; colors and gradients: paint the selection (and the defaults) as paint.setFill/paint.setStroke, a gradient fitting each object; a spot color links to the document's spot swatch of its ink's name, added when the document has none of that colour (a name taken by another colour gets a number), one undo step; patterns: add the pattern and its swatch to the document (a name the document gives another pattern gets a number; the same pattern is reused) and paint the selection (and the defaults) with it, one undo step; charStyle/paraStyle: add the style to the document (a name taken by different attributes gets a number; a character style's color linked to a swatch that isn't a global or spot swatch of the document keeps the color it shows, unlinked) and apply it to the selected text, one undo step → {kind, ids?, style?}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs"}
  {:id "links.embed",
   :label "Embed Image",
   :params
   "{ids?: [image or placed document ids] (default: the selected linked ones)} break the links (the Links panel's Break Link): images keep the linked files' pixels in the document; a placed document becomes an editable copy of its art, as placing its file without link gives (its symbols, patterns, swatches and images joining the document). An image whose file can't be found and that shows the saved preview, or a placed document whose file can't be read or changed, stays linked: relink or update it first. An image placed from a DCS file can't be embedded (an error, and nothing changes). One undo step → {embedded: [ids], missing: [ids]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/links.rs"}
  {:id "links.goTo",
   :label "Go To Link",
   :params
   "{id?} select image or placed document `id` (default: the first selected one); the Links panel scrolls it into view → {id, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1], onCanvas: true}; one in opacity-mask art or in the art of a symbol, graph design, pattern or stored brush has no place of its own on the canvas: the selection is cleared → {id, onCanvas: false, owner} (owner as links.list gives it)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/links.rs"}
  {:id "links.placementOptions",
   :label "Placement Options",
   :params
   "{ids?: [image or placed document ids] (default: the selected ones), preserve?: transforms|bounds (default)|fileDimensions|fit|fill, align?: topLeft|top|topRight|left|center (default)|right|bottomLeft|bottom|bottomRight (where the new art sits; not for bounds), clip?: false (clip it to the old bounds where it is larger)} how a file read again (links.relink, links.update) takes each image's place: transforms keeps its scale (relative to each file's 100% size), rotation and position; bounds stretches it into the old bounds; fileDimensions puts it at 100%, unrotated; fit and fill scale it proportionally to fit inside or cover the old bounds. Without options → {placement} of the first image; else one undo step → {ids, placement}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/links.rs"}
  {:id "links.relink",
   :label "Relink",
   :params
   "{ids?: [image or placed document ids] (default: the selected ones; with folder and nothing selected, every missing link), path | folder, scope?: selected (default: ids) | all (ids and every other object linked to the same file as one of them, in the layers, opacity-mask art, symbols, graph designs, patterns and the art of stored brushes) | missingInFolder (with path: ids, then every other missing link whose file name is in path's folder, each to the file of its name there; names not there are in notFound; with copy, only images are looked for) | each (with paths), paths?: [{ids, path}] (with scope each, in place of ids, path and folder: each link to its own file; an id in two entries is an error), copy?: false (with path or paths, for images of a saved document: copy the file into the document's folder and link to the copy; the names Name.png, Name 2.png … Name 99.png are tried in turn until one is free, which gets the copy, or is a file with the same contents, which is used; an error for a DCS file that reads plate files of its own), preserve?: transforms|bounds|fileDimensions|fit|fill (how the new file takes each image's place this time, as links.placementOptions describes; default: each image's Placement Options; fit keeps the new file's aspect ratio inside the old bounds: Replace)} link images (or placed documents, each showing the same artboard or page of the new file) to the file at path, or each to the file of its link's name in folder; embedded images become linked; each keeps its bounds. One undo step → {relinked: [ids], notFound: [file names], copied?: [{from, to}], kept?: [{from, to}] (with copy; to is the file name alone when the document's folder is outside the automation read roots), warnings?: (as links.update's)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/links.rs"}
  {:id "links.unembed",
   :label "Unembed",
   :params
   "{id?: an embedded image (default: the one selected), path?} write the image's pixels to the file at path (PNG, JPEG, GIF or WebP as stored, other images as PNG; a path ending in .png/.jpg/.jpeg/.gif/.webp/.tif/.tiff/.bmp converts them) and link the image to it, keeping its bounds. One undo step → {id, path}; no path → {name, dataBase64} (nothing changes: there is no file to link to)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/links.rs"}
  {:id "links.update",
   :label "Update Links",
   :params
   "{ids?: [image or placed document ids] (default: the linked images whose file was modified or is showing its preview, and placed documents whose file was modified)} read their linked files again; each keeps its bounds. Images and placed documents inside symbols, graph designs, patterns, opacity masks and the art of stored brushes have ids of their own, as links.list gives them; those that show the same content as one read again are read again too. One undo step → {updated: [ids], missing: [ids], warnings?: [a DCS file's spot plate whose ink a swatch of the document already names, as file.place warns]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/links.rs"}
  {:id "links.updateChanged",
   :label "Update Changed Links",
   :params
   "{} read again the active document's linked files that changed on disk since they were last seen (size or modification time), whatever Preferences → File Handling → Update Links says; the desktop app looks every two seconds and follows that preference. Files seen for the first time are only remembered. One undo step → {updated: [ids], ask: [], modified: []}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/links.rs"}
  {:id "livePaint.expand",
   :label "Expand",
   :params
   "{id?, ids?: [id…] (instead of id)} turn Live Paint groups into plain groups of the faces and edges that draw, with all their fill and stroke rows: a shown face or edge with an opacity above 0 and a shown fill or stroke row that has paint and an opacity above 0 (a stroke also a weight above 0), whichever row is on top → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "livePaint.fill",
   :label "Live Paint Bucket",
   :params
   "{group?: id | ids?|id?: [id…] (paths to make live first, as livePaint.make does), point: [x,y], points?: [[x,y]…] (a drag polyline starting at point; 1 to 4096 finite canvas points; fills every crossed face of the same group), continuation?: [[[x,y]…]…] (further path chunks of 1 to 4096 finite canvas points each; each starts at the preceding chunk's last point; requires points), scope?: \"one\" (default: the face alone) | \"connected\" (a double-click: also each face reached across edges that are hidden or draw no stroke, as a flood from the face; a stroked edge, a hidden face or a Gap Detection gap stops it) | \"samePaint\" (a triple-click: also every face of the group whose fill is match; \"connected\" and \"samePaint\" are refused with points), match?: paint (as the document stores it, the `fill` of a face's appearance; scope samePaint only; default: the face's fill), color?|swatch?|gradient?|none? (default: current fill; a color in #rrggbbaa or #rgba is refused), tint?: 0..100, keepModel?: bool (both as paint.setFill)} fill the face containing point, skipping hidden faces: each face reached has its fills replaced by one fill with the paint, shown, fully opaque and blending normally, in the place of its topmost fill (none leaves one fill of none), and its strokes and its own opacity stay as they are; when every face it reaches already has only that one fill, nothing changes (no undo step, and the recent colors stay as they are) → {group, face, count (faces reached)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "livePaint.gapOptions",
   :label "Gap Options",
   :params
   "{id?, ids?: [id…] (instead of id; default: the selected Live Paint groups), detect?: bool (Gap Detection: paint stops at gaps up to size wide), size?: \"small\" (3 pt) | \"medium\" (6 pt) | \"large\" (12 pt) | pt (custom, over 0 up to 72) (Paint Stops At), color?: #rrggbb or a layer color's name such as \"Red\" (Gap Preview Color; a hex color with an alpha part, #rrggbbaa or #rgba, is an error), closeGaps?: bool (add an unpainted path across each gap up to size wide to the group's paths)} set the Gap Options of Live Paint groups (what is not given stays as it was; a group starts with detect false, small and Red) and make their faces again, keeping their paint; when every group already has the options and closeGaps finds no gap, nothing changes (no undo step) → {ids, faces, gaps: [[x0,y0,x1,y1]…] (the gaps up to size wide that no path closes, from a loose end of a path to where it closes to; detect closes them for paint), closed (paths added)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "livePaint.make",
   :label "Make",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} build a Live Paint group from the selected paths (paths, compound paths and groups of them; type, images and other objects are refused, nothing changes); each covered face starts with the fill rows that draw (shown, with paint and an opacity above 0) of its front-most covering source that has one and an opacity above 0, and each edge with the stroke rows that draw (also a weight above 0) of its source, in order with their settings and with that source's opacity and blending mode (on a path cut into several edges, dashes go on along the path with the lengths set, without the fit of dashes aligned to corners and path ends, arrowheads stay at its own ends, and a width profile or brush stays only on an edge that runs the whole path); a face or edge given no such row has one unpainted row; with a Live Paint group among them, add the others to it as livePaint.merge does; a Live Paint group alone has nothing to add, so it is selected and nothing changes (no undo step) → {id, faces, edges}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "livePaint.merge",
   :label "Merge",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} add the other selected paths (compound paths, groups of paths and Live Paint groups too; type, images and other objects are refused, nothing changes) to the bottom-most Live Paint group, keeping its id, its paint and its own properties (name, lock, visibility, transparency, appearance, opacity mask, graphic style link); a Live Paint group alone has nothing to add, so it is selected and nothing changes (no undo step) → {id, faces, edges}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "livePaint.release",
   :label "Release",
   :params
   "{id?, ids?: [id…] (instead of id)} replace Live Paint groups with their original paths → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "livePaint.strokeEdge",
   :label "Live Paint Bucket (Stroke)",
   :params
   "{group: id, point: [x,y], color?|swatch?|none? (default: current stroke), width?: pt (default: current weight), tolerance?: pt (4), points?: [[x,y]…] (a drag polyline starting at point; 1 to 4096 finite canvas points; also paints every edge of the group, hidden edges skipped, that the polyline crosses or comes within 0.0001 pt of), continuation?: [[[x,y]…]…] (further path chunks of 1 to 4096 finite canvas points each; each starts at the preceding chunk's last point; requires points), scope?: \"one\" (default: the edge alone) | \"connected\" (a double-click: also each edge joined to it, end to end, through edges that draw with stroke paint match) | \"samePaint\" (a triple-click: also every edge of the group that draws with stroke paint match; \"connected\" and \"samePaint\" are refused with points), match?: paint (as the document stores it; scope connected or samePaint only; default: the stroke paint the edge draws with; an edge draws with the paint of its topmost stroke that is shown, with paint, above 0 pt and not fully transparent, and with none when the edge is fully transparent or has no such stroke), through?: [id…] (scope connected only; at most 4096 of the group's edges, each given once, counted as drawing with stroke paint match whatever they draw with, such as another edge a double-click's clicks painted; any other id is an error), tint?: 0..100, keepModel?: bool (both as paint.setFill)} paint the edge nearest point, skipping hidden edges: each edge reached has its strokes replaced by one stroke with the paint and width, shown, fully opaque and blending normally, in the place of its topmost stroke and with the dashes, caps and arrowheads of its topmost shown stroke (a new stroke above the fills when it has none; none leaves one stroke of none), and its fills stay as they are; when every edge it reaches already has only that one stroke (at any width for none), nothing changes (no undo step, and the recent colors stay as they are) → {group, edge, count (edges reached)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "node.move",
   :label "Reorder",
   :params
   "{id, parent?: id (null = top level), index} put a row at `index` (0 = bottom) of `parent` (layers only at the top level or in layers; an Intertwine group takes and gives up members as layer.move does), deselecting every selected object left hidden or locked (the key object too)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/layer.rs"}
  {:id "object.align",
   :label "Align",
   :params
   "{horizontal?: \"left\"|\"center\"|\"right\", vertical?: \"top\"|\"center\"|\"bottom\", to?: \"selection\"|\"artboard\"|\"key\" (default: the key object when the selection has one, select.key, else the selection; a key guide, select.key {guide}, stays put and the objects line up on its line: a vertical guide sets where left, center and right go and vertical alignment leaves them, a horizontal one the other way round; aligning to the key, the other selected ruler guides move too: a vertical guide to the key's left edge, center or right edge, a horizontal one to its top, center or bottom; aligning to the artboard moves selected guides to its edges too (#3463), and with only guides selected aligning to the selection moves them to their collective bounds), artboard?: index (0-based; with to: \"artboard\", the artboard to align to; the app passes the active one; default: the artboard under the center of the selection, else the first), bounds?: \"preview\"|\"geometric\" (default: the Use Preview Bounds preference; preview bounds take in strokes, geometry effects and projected 3D art), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles)} With anchor points selected (Direct Selection), the points align instead: to their own bounds, to the artboard (#1180), or, aligning to the key with a key anchor (select.key {id, anchor}), to the key anchor, which stays put",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
