   :label "Pencil",
   :params
   "{points: [[x,y]…] or [[x,y,pressure]…] or [[x,y,pressure,tiltX,tiltY,rotation]…] (pen pressure 0..1: the stroke keeps it, for Calligraphic and Scatter brushes with Pressure variation; a point without one presses fully. Pen tilt in degrees, each −90..90, x positive leaning right and y leaning down the page, and barrel rotation in degrees clockwise, 0..360: the stroke keeps how far the pen leaned, which way and how far its barrel turned, for brushes with Tilt, Bearing and Rotation variation; null for what a point lacks. A pressure, tilt or rotation outside its range, or a point array of more than six numbers, is an error), fidelity?: pt (1.5; from 0.000015625 (0.01 / 640) to 100 / 0.0313 (about 3194.89), the Pencil's and the Paintbrush's 0.01 to 100 px Fidelity at the highest and the lowest zoom; a value outside that range is an error. The tools send their Fidelity in pixels divided by the zoom, kept within the range), fit?: bool (true; false: the points are joined by straight segments, as the Pencil previews a stroke with Live curve fitting off), closed?, style?: \"pencil\" (default) | \"brush\", fill?: bool, keepSelected?: bool (true: the drawn or continued path is selected; false: a new path leaves nothing selected, and a continued or redrawn one is deselected while the rest of the selection stays), extend?: {id, end?: \"end\" (default) | \"start\"}, connect?: {id, end: \"start\"|\"end\"}, redraw?: {id, within?: pt (12)}} fit a freehand stroke → {id}. extend continues the path from that end, and closes it when `closed` is true (left out, when the stroke ends within four Fidelities of the path's other end, 6 to 400 pt); with connect, the stroke ends on that end of another path's last open subpath and joins it on, in one path with the extended path's appearance (the other path is removed when nothing of it is left); redraw (Edit Selected Paths) replaces the section of the path between where the stroke starts and ends, each within `within` of one subpath (the shorter way round a closed one), and draws a new path when the stroke doesn't end on it. Any other style, extend end or connect end is an error, and nothing changes",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "path.insertAnchor",
   :label "Add Anchor Point",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?, segment, t: 0..1} add an anchor at t on the segment → {anchor}; the direct-selected anchors and selected segments keep the same points (a selected segment it splits stays selected as its two halves), and a path that isn't selected becomes the selection with the new anchor direct-selected",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.join",
   :label "Join",
   :params
   "{ids?: [path, ...] (default: the selected paths; a compound path ID expands to its open member paths), subpaths?: [usize, usize] (which subpaths to join), ends?: [\"first\"|\"last\", \"first\"|\"last\"] (which end of each path to join, for two paths/subpaths; default without ids: direct-selected ends if any, else the nearest pair; default with ids: the nearest pair), to?: \"corner\"|\"smooth\" (the joined anchor: corner retracts both handles, smooth pulls handles in line with the neighbours)} join two or more open paths/subpaths into one (the first keeps its id, selected), or close a single open path; without ids, direct-selected anchors lying on one another along a path merge into one anchor instead",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.joinScrub",
   :label "Join",
   :params
   "{points: [[x,y]…] (pen values after x and y are checked as path.freehand checks them and do not change the join), tolerance?: pt (12)} join the open-path endpoints scrubbed over, or trim two crossing open paths whose overhanging ends are scrubbed and join them at the crossing → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "path.knife",
   :label "Knife",
   :params
   "{points: [[x,y]…] (pen values after x and y are checked as path.freehand checks them and do not change the cut)} cut closed shapes (selected, or all when nothing is selected) along the polyline → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "path.lineCut",
   :label "Line Cut",
   :params
   "{from: [x,y], to: [x,y]} split the selected paths and compound paths along the line through both points, extended across the art: filled shapes become their pieces on each side (holes kept), open paths split where they cross; as one undo step → {ids, removed: 0}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/cut.rs"}
  {:id "path.mirrorCut",
   :label "Mirror & Cut",
   :params
   "{axis?: \"vertical\"|\"horizontal\"|\"free\" (vertical), from?: [x,y], to?: [x,y] (free: the axis through both; vertical/horizontal: the axis through `from`, default the selection's centre), keep?: \"left\"|\"right\"|\"top\"|\"bottom\" (the side kept; default left, or top for a horizontal-ish axis)} cut the selected paths and compound paths at the axis, reflect the kept half across it and join both halves into one closed shape (open paths are joined where they meet the axis); art wholly on the other side is deleted, as one undo step → {ids, removed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/cut.rs"}
  {:id "path.moveAnchor",
   :label "Move Anchor Point",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?, anchor, x, y} move one anchor to (x, y), its handles with it",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.moveAnchors",
   :label "Move Anchors",
   :params
   "{dx, dy, patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the objects that move whole; default: prefs transformPatternTiles)} move direct-selected anchors (whole paths if fully selected); refused while an object of a symbol instance's art is selected",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.rectCut",
   :label "Rectangle Cut",
   :params
   "{rect: [x, y, width, height]} or {from: [x,y], to: [x,y]} (opposite corners) crop the selected paths and compound paths to the rectangle as real geometry (not a clipping mask): filled shapes are intersected with it, open paths keep their parts inside, art wholly outside is deleted; as one undo step → {ids, removed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/cut.rs"}
  {:id "path.removeAnchor",
   :label "Delete Anchor Point",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?, anchor, curvature?} remove one anchor, re-fitting the curve (with curvature: true, the curve where it was follows the remaining anchors, as the Curvature tool curves its points)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "path.removeAnchors",
   :label "Remove Anchor Points",
   :params
   "{} remove the direct-selected anchors without opening their paths, refitting the curve round each; the anchor after each removed one is selected, so running it again goes on along the path → {removedObjects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "path.reshape",
   :label "Reshape",
   :params
   "{id, x, y, dx, dy, tol=3, focal?: [[subpath, anchor]…], radius?} Reshape tool: grab the path at (x, y) (adding an anchor there unless one is within tol) and drag it by (dx, dy). The grabbed anchor and the anchors in focal are focal points and move by the whole drag. Anchors that are not direct-selected stay in place (a path selected whole, or not selected, has every anchor selected), and so do an open path's two ends unless they are focal points. A selected anchor between two focal points moves whole; one between a focal point and an anchor that stays takes a share of the drag that falls smoothly from 1 at the focal point to 0 at the anchor that stays, by its distance along the path's control polygon. A closed subpath with every anchor selected moves whole; a subpath with no focal point does not move. With radius, only the grabbed point's subpath changes: anchors follow with a smooth falloff over radius, measured along the path (0 or more), whatever the selection; focal and radius cannot be used together. Without focal (or with focal null) and without radius, the earlier rule applies: the selection does not matter, an open path stretches from the grabbed point to its two ends, and on a closed path the anchors follow with the falloff over half the diagonal of the subpath's bounding box; the Reshape tool always sends focal",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.reshapeSegment",
   :label "Reshape Segment",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?, segment, t, dx, dy, perpendicular?: bool} bend a segment so the point at t moves by (dx, dy); with perpendicular (Shift), both handles stand at right angles to the line between its anchors at one length, and the point at t lies as far from that line as the moved point does",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "path.reverse",
   :label "Reverse Path Direction",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, subpath?: usize (reverse only this subpath of each path, 0 included; default: every subpath), reversed?: bool (true: every subpath runs counter-clockwise on screen, false: clockwise, the Attributes panel's Reverse Path Direction On / Off; omitted: flip each path; with subpath, the direction is not read: that subpath is flipped)} the paths in ids or the selection (groups and compound paths: the paths inside), as one undo step; when every subpath of a path or compound path turns alike, its strokes' width profiles (sides swapped) and pen pressure, tilt, bearing and rotation turn with it, so they draw as before → {changed: paths}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.setAnchors",
   :label "Set Anchors",
   :params
   "{id, subpaths: [{anchors: [{x,y,in?,out?}], closed}]} replace a path's geometry",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.setFillRule",
   :label "Fill Rule",
   :params
   "{rule: \"nonZero\"|\"evenOdd\", ids?|id?} the fill rule of the paths and compound paths in ids or the selection (groups: those inside), as one undo step → {changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/attributes.rs"}
  {:id "path.setHandle",
   :label "Move Direction Handle",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?, anchor, which: \"in\"|\"out\", x, y, independent?: bool}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/path.rs"}
  {:id "path.smoothRegion",
   :label "Smooth",
   :params
   "{points: [[x,y]…] (pen values after x and y are checked as path.freehand checks them and do not change the smoothing), radius?: pt (12), fidelity?: pt (2.5; kept within 0.000078125 and about 3195, the Smooth tool's 0.05 to 100 px at the highest and the lowest zoom: the tool sends its Fidelity in screen pixels divided by the zoom)} smooth selected paths near the drag, keeping a corner where the path turns by more than 57.5° at the anchor and over radius and twice radius on either side → {ids, before, after}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "path.split",
   :label "Split Path",
   :params
   "{id, subpath?, segment, t: 0–1 (0.5)} or {id, subpath?, anchor}: closed paths open there, open paths become two; one of the two new end points is left selected; the paths keep the source's fill and stroke settings except that every stroke's alignment becomes Center (in a path of several subpaths, the other subpaths' strokes too) → {ids}. A t outside 0–1 is refused with an error, and nothing changes",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/commands.rs"}
  {:id "pattern.delete",
   :label "Delete Pattern",
   :params
   "{name} delete a pattern and its swatches; every paint of it, new art's fill and stroke included, becomes none → {unpainted: the number of document paints cleared}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/patterncmds.rs"}
  {:id "pattern.options",
   :label "Pattern Options",
   :params
   "{name? (default: the pattern being edited), newName? (trimmed; blank: the name is kept), tileType?, brickOffset?, width?, height?, hSpacing?, vSpacing?, sizeTileToArt?: bool, moveTileWithArt?: bool (in pattern editing mode, a move of all of the tile art moves the tile with it; off for a new pattern), overlap?: {h: left|right, v: top|bottom}, copies?: 3|5|7|9, dimCopies?: %, showTileEdge?: bool, showSwatchBounds?: bool (outline the part of the tiling the swatch repeats, dashed)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/patterncmds.rs"}
  {:id "pattern.transform",
   :label "Transform Patterns",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, matrix: [a,b,c,d,e,f]} transform only the pattern placement of the objects' pattern paints (Transform Patterns)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/patterncmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.attach",
   :label "Attach to Active Plane",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, plane?: left|right|ground (default: the active plane)} project the objects onto the plane",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.draw",
   :label "Draw in Perspective",
   :params
   "{command: shape.* id, params, plane?, snap?: bool (default: Snap to Grid), at?: [x, y] (a point of the plane the shape lies on, as the tool gives it)} run a shape command and attach the result to the plane (snapping its corners to gridlines within a quarter cell)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.editText",
   :label "Edit Text",
   :params
   "{id? (default: the selected type)} Object › Perspective › Edit Text: show type in perspective flat where it is drawn, in isolation mode, to edit it (text.* commands, the Type tool); exiting isolation (object.exitIsolation, Esc) projects it again; refused while an opacity mask is edited → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.define",
   :label "Define Perspective Grid",
   :params
   "{name?: preset name (\"\" = custom), kind?: 1|2|3, units?: unit name (points, pixels, inches, centimeters, millimeters…), scale?: [artboard, real world], gridline?: gridline every, angle?: viewing angle (0–90°), distance?: viewing distance, horizonHeight?: above the ground level, thirdVp?: [x right, y up] from the centre of vision (3-point), leftColor?, rightColor?, groundColor?: \"#rrggbb\", opacity?: 0–100} lengths are real-world lengths in `units` at `scale`; missing fields keep the grid's (see perspective.grid.get define). Only what changes changes: a new type, angle or distance moves the vanishing points around the station point. One undo step → the new define fields",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/perspgrid.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.lock",
   :label "Lock Grid",
   :params
   "{on?: bool} (no param toggles) View › Perspective Grid › Lock Grid: the grid's widgets can't be dragged (the Plane Switching Widget still works). View state: not an undo step → {on}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/perspgrid.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.lockStation",
   :label "Lock Station Point",
   :params
   "{on?: bool} (no param toggles) dragging one vanishing point moves the other around the station point (the viewing angle turns, the viewer stays). View state: not an undo step → {on}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/perspgrid.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.preset",
   :label "Perspective Grid Preset",
   :params
   "{kind: 1|2|3 (its normal view) | name: a preset (see perspective.presets.list)} reset the grid to the preset fitted to the first artboard (and show it; attached objects stay attached). No undo step when the document already holds that grid; when only whether it shows or its active plane differs, those are set without one",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.rulers",
   :label "Show Rulers",
   :params
   "{on?: bool} (no param toggles) a ruler up the line where the planes meet, in the grid's units at its scale. View state: not an undo step → {on}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/perspgrid.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.set",
   :label "Define Perspective Grid",
   :params
   "{kind?: 1|2|3, origin?: [x,y], horizon?, vpLeft?, vpRight?, vpVertical?: [x,y], distance?, cell?, extent?, height?, visible?, plane?, leftOffset?, rightOffset?, groundOffset?: pt (planes moved along their normals), reproject?: bool, …the other fields of the grid as its reply lists them} merge into the document's grid. Objects in perspective stay where they are, as in the reference app; with reproject they move with the grid (each keeps its place on its plane)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.show",
   :label "Show Perspective Grid",
   :params
   "{visible?: bool} (no param toggles). View state: not an undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.grid.snap",
   :label "Snap to Grid",
   :params
   "{on?: bool} (no param toggles) art drawn or moved in perspective lands on gridlines within a quarter cell (on by default). View state: not an undo step → {on}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/perspgrid.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.move",
   :label "Move in Perspective",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, from: [x,y], to: [x,y], plane?, copy?: bool (move copies, as Alt-dragging does), perpendicular?: bool (move along the plane's normal instead, as pressing 5 while dragging does), snap?: bool (default: View › Perspective Grid › Snap to Grid), constrain?: bool (default false; constrain each in-plane move to its plane's nearest axis or 45° diagonal)} slide objects within their own planes (unattached objects attach to `plane`/the active plane first); snapping pulls the nearer edge of the first plane's joint bounds toward a gridline within a quarter cell while preserving the constrained direction, and moves every object on that plane, at any depth, by the same plane offset; Transform Again repeats it",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.nudge",
   :label "Nudge in Perspective",
   :params
   "{dx, dy: arrow direction (-1, 0 or 1), big?: bool (×10), copy?: bool} move the selection in perspective by the keyboard increment, as the arrow keys do with the Perspective Selection tool → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.plane.infer",
   :label "Automatic Plane Positioning",
   :params
   "{at?: [x, y], tolerance?: pt around `at` (default 6), clear?: bool} with `at` on an anchor point of shown art in perspective, or on a gridline intersection of a plane that shows, the active plane moves through that point for now and the other planes hide (the Perspective Selection tool: Shift held over one with no button down). An anchor point within reach wins over an intersection, and perspective.widget.options turns either off. Making another plane active (perspective.plane.set) brings that plane through the same point. The plane goes back to its place when an object is drawn on it or attached to it (perspective.draw, perspective.attach, an object brought into perspective by perspective.move or perspective.transform), when a plane is moved (perspective.plane.move, perspective.plane.matchObject), when the grid hides or no plane is active, when the file is opened again, and with `clear` (Escape with the Perspective Selection tool). View state: not an undo step; no params reads it → {active, plane, offset: where the active plane is, point?: [x, y, z] in the grid's frame, source?: anchor|gridline (what `at` found; absent when nothing was within reach)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/perspgrid.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.plane.matchObject",
   :label "Move Plane to Match Object",
   :params
   "{id? (default: the first selected object)} move the plane the object is attached to onto the object and make it the active plane → {plane, offset}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.plane.move",
   :label "Move Plane",
   :params
   "{plane?: left|right|ground (default: the active plane), offset?: pt (where along its normal; 0 is its place in the grid's definition) | by?: pt, objects?: none|move|copy (default none: the objects on the plane stay; move: they move with it, as Shift-dragging a plane widget does; copy: copies of them do, as Alt-dragging does)} → {plane, offset, ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.plane.set",
   :label "Active Perspective Plane",
   :params
   "{plane: left|right|ground|none} Plane Switching widget. View state: not an undo step",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.release",
   :label "Release with Perspective",
   :params "{ids?|id?} detach from the grid (geometry unchanged)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "perspective.transform",
   :label "Transform in Perspective",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, matrix: [a,b,c,d,e,f] (affine map in plane coordinates, points: u along the plane, v up or away), depth?: pt to move along the plane's normal (default 0), copy?: bool, plane?} transform objects within their own planes (Perspective Selection tool handles; unattached objects attach to `plane`/the active plane first); Transform Again repeats it → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "plugin.run",
   :label "Run Plug-in",
   :params
   "{id, params?: {…} (the plug-in's parameters; or give them as top-level keys; missing ones take their defaults, see plugin.info), ids?: [object id] (left out or null: the selection), …the plug-in's parameters as top-level keys} run an object filter on the selected paths and compound paths (inside selected groups and layers too; hidden, locked, guide and clipping paths, compound paths that clip a clip group and paths inside a group that clips one are left out): it may change, delete or add objects, as one undo step; the result is selected, except the objects it locked or made guides. A filter whose manifest lists inputs (type, image, symbolInstance; it lists doc.read in permissions, so plugin.install needs grant) is also given the selected objects of those kinds to read, in paint order from the bottom, with at most 16 MiB of pixels and 16 MiB of type runs per run (an object that doesn't fit what the objects before it left comes with pixelsOmitted or truncated; an image that reaches the decoder counts toward the pixels even when decoding fails); every object counts toward the input's half of the plug-in's memory cap, ids, bounds, transforms and names included, and an object whose fields besides its pixels and runs don't fit fails the run with a memory-budget error naming it and its size (a path or compound path fails it with the memory-budget error for a selection too large to hand over), and more than 100,000 of these objects fail it with an object-budget error: its output returns each as {id} or exactly as given, or the run is refused and nothing changes. With nothing selected it gets no objects (generators add theirs to the current layer). A filter with a commandAllowlist runs the commands it names while it runs (vc_call, see docs/plugins.md): its calls and its output are one undo step, and a run that fails or makes a call that fails changes nothing → {plugin, ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/plugin.rs"}
  {:id "print.setup",
   :label "Print Setup",
   :params
   "{preset?: name ([Default] or a saved print preset, any case: print.presets.list; its settings replace the document's, as choosing it in the Print dialog does), settings?: {copies: 1 (1–999), collate: true, reverse, artboards: all|range|ignore (all the art as one page), range: \"1-3, 5\" (1-based, with artboards: range), skipBlank (leave out artboards with no art that prints), media: letter|legal|tabloid|a3|a4|a5|a6|b4|b5|b4 (jis)|b5 (jis)|b6 (jis)|japanese postcard|japanese double postcard|japanese envelope #3|japanese envelope #4|kaku #2|kaku #3|yonroku-ban|custom (a paper is named by its id or its dialog label, any case and spacing, so `B5 (JIS)` works; b4 and b5 stay the ISO 216 sizes, 250 × 353 and 176 × 250 mm, and the JIS sizes are b4 (jis) 257 × 364 mm, b5 (jis) 182 × 257 mm and b6 (jis) 128 × 182 mm), width, height (custom paper, 72–14400 pt), orientation: portrait|landscape|portraitFlipped|landscapeFlipped, autoRotate: true (turn the paper to each artboard; orientation ignored), transverse (the page a quarter turn on the paper), printLayers: visiblePrintable|visible|all (template layers never print), placement: {origin: topLeft|top|topRight|left|center|right|bottomLeft|bottom|bottomRight (the point of the printed area, the artboard with its bleed and marks, on the same point of the imageable area), x, y (pt, right and down)}, scaling: none|fit|custom|tileFull|tileImageable, scale: {width: 100, height: 100 (1–1000 % with custom and tiling), linked: true (width and height stay equal: give one and the other follows, and turning it on sets the height to the width; a different width and height without linked turn it off, and with linked: true, or linked: null over a linked scale, are an error; a saved scale without linked reads it as false)}, overlap: 0 (pt between tiles), tileRange: \"\" (1-based tiles across then down; empty: all), copiesPerSheet: false (not with tiling: as many copies of each artboard, with its bleed and marks, as fit the imageable area, across then down, not turned; the placement places the grid; an artboard that doesn't fit prints one copy per sheet, with a warning), gutter: 0 (pt between copies, 0–720), margin: 0 (pt the device can't print around the paper: the imageable area is inside it), marks: {trim, registration, colorBars, pageInfo, kind: roman|japanese, weight: 0.25, offset: 6} (as document.exportPdf, at the paper's scale; page information adds the tile and the ink), bleed: {useDocument: true (the document's bleed, document.setup), top, bottom, left, right} (pt), output: {mode: composite|separations (one gray page per ink that prints), emulsion: up|down (down mirrors), image: positive|negative, spotsToProcess, overprintBlack: false (separations: solid 100% K or 100% gray fills, strokes and characters, to within half a percent, overprint in the printed copy, gradients when every stop is (every point of a freeform one); rich, RGB, spot-linked and lighter blacks are not marked, and paints already set to overprint keep it; composite ignores it), inks: [{name: \"Cyan\"|…|a spot swatch, print: true, frequency (lpi, default 60), angle (screen angle, degrees counter-clockwise as PostScript setscreen takes it; default C 15, M 75, Y 0, K 45, spots 45), convertToProcess: false (a spot ink only: it prints on the process plates, with no plate of its own, and its print, frequency and angle are kept for when it prints as a spot ink again; spotsToProcess converts every spot ink whatever it says)}]}, graphics: {autoFlatness: true, flatness: 1 (0.2–100), fonts: none|subset|complete}, color: {intent: perceptual|relativeColorimetric|saturation|absoluteColorimetric, preserveNumbers: true (CMYK colors keep their values), profile: \"\" (the printer profile, an RGB or CMYK one: composite PDF colors are converted to it with the intent, separations separate with a CMYK one; empty: as they are)}, advanced: {printAsBitmap (composite pages print as one image each, at the document's raster effects resolution, or lower for a page larger than 64 Mpx or 32,768 px a side), overprints: preserve|discard|simulate (composite output; preserve writes them to overprint (/OP), simulate prints them as Overprint Preview shows them; separations always keep them), flattenerPreset: \"\" (a flattener preset, built-in or saved: transparency is flattened before printing; empty: it prints live; PostScript defaults to medium)}, tileOrigin: {placed: false, x, y} (where the Print Tiling tool put the pages: print.tiling.set)}} store the print settings with the document, over the ones it has or the preset's (null keeps a value), as one undo step; no settings or preset → {settings} (the current ones, defaults if never set up)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/print.rs"}
  {:id "print.tiling.set",
   :label "Print Tiling",
   :params
   "{origin: [x, y] (document point: the top-left corner of the first page's imageable area), artboard? (0-based: the artboard it is measured from; default the printed artboard containing origin, its edges included, else the first; ignored with artboards: ignore)} | {reset: true} place the printed pages as the Print Tiling tool does, saved with the print settings (tileOrigin: {placed, x, y}, from the artboard's top-left corner; it replaces the placement, and tiles start there), as one undo step; reset → the placement places them again → {tileOrigin}",
