   "{cx, cy, radius1, radius2, points=5, rotation?: deg clockwise (0: a point straight up)} → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/create.rs"}
  {:id "shapeBuilder.merge",
   :label "Shape Builder",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?: [id…] (default: selection), points: [[x,y]…] (drag path; one point = click; may be left out with rect), rect?: [x, y, width, height] (Shift-drag marquee from where the drag started, x and y, to x+width and y+height; width and height may be negative: touches every region whose outline crosses the rectangle or has an anchor inside it and the region holding the whole rectangle, the region under x, y comes first and the one under the opposite corner comes next; with points, it also touches the regions along them; for pickColorFrom, x, y is the drag's first point and the opposite corner is its last), erase?: bool (erase mode, Alt: deletes the regions touched, and the pieces of open paths that cut regions and the edges (outline pieces between the points where paths meet; see shapeBuilder.regions) within tolerance, except that a point in a region no more than twice the tolerance across there touches the region; a deleted edge opens its path there, and edges bounding a deleted region go with it; what is left of each path keeps its look, with gradients fitted to its bounds kept where they were on it, its name, opacity mask and attributes, and its fill rule unless merged regions shaped it), splitStroke?: false (In Merge Mode, Clicking Stroke Splits the Path; not with erase or rect: when the one point of a click is within tolerance of a stroke, the path that stroke is on splits in two instead of a merge: the path keeps the rest of it, and a copy of the path holding the run of it from the anchor or crossing point before the click to the one after it, in the path's direction, goes directly above it; both keep the path's gradients where they were on it; the other objects stay as they are; with pickColorFrom \"swatches\" or fill, the run's stroke takes that paint; a path in a Live Paint group or a Shaper Group does not split, and nor does a path the run is all of, such as a lone line, or all but 0.05 pt or less of (a ten-thousandth of the larger side of a path over 500 pt)), tolerance?: pt (2, erase or splitStroke), gap?: pt (0–72; 0: Gap Detection off), openFilledAsClosed?: true (Consider Open Filled Paths as Closed: a filled open path bounds a region as if an invisible edge closed it, where filled means any fill row is shown, painted and above 0% opacity, whichever row is on top; false: it cuts the regions it crosses like an unfilled one), pickColorFrom?: \"artwork\" (default: the merged shape takes the look of the front-most object under the first point, else under the last point, else of the front-most object) | \"swatches\" (the current fill, with the rest of the look of the front-most object over the first region the drag touches that an object covers, else of the front-most object), fill?: \"#rrggbb\" | {color|swatch|gradient|none} (overrides pickColorFrom)} replaces the paths it uses where they are; other selected objects (type, hidden or locked objects, clipping paths) stay, and a group goes only when it is left empty → {ids (selected after: each selected object still there, or what took its place), merged, regions, lines, edges (counts deleted, merged or split), split?: id (the run split off, after a split)}; after a split, ids are the roots, with the rest and the run in place of the path when it was one",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/buildcmds.rs"}
  {:id "shaper.expand",
   :label "Expand Shaper Group",
   :params
   "{id? (default: selection)} keep the visible result as ordinary paths → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shaper.rs"}
  {:id "shaper.release",
   :label "Release Shaper Group",
   :params
   "{id? (default: selection)} restore the original paths → {ids}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shaper.rs"}
  {:id "shaper.releaseSource",
   :label "Remove from Shaper Group",
   :params
   "{source: id, group?: id (default: the Shaper Group that holds `source`)} take one original shape out of its Shaper Group: it becomes a path just above the group, keeps its look and is selected, and Construction mode ends; the group's result is computed again from the shapes left, and a group left with none is removed. In Construction mode, a Selection-tool move that ends with an original shape wholly outside the bounds the group's original shapes had does the same in the move's undo step (object.transform's `releaseOutside`) → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shaper.rs"}
  {:id "shaper.scribble",
   :label "Shaper",
   :params
   "{points: [[x,y]…], ids?: [id…] (default: nearby art), tolerance?: pt (4)} interior scribbles remove fills; scribbles through several regions merge with the origin fill; ending outside removes fills and boundary strokes; outside scribbles erase stroke pieces. Originals remain editable → {id, regions, strokes}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shaper.rs"}
  {:id "shaper.select",
   :label "Select Shaper Face",
   :params
   "{point: [x,y], source?: bool, tolerance?: pt (3)} click selects a group, then a face; with the group or one of its faces selected, a click within tolerance of an original shape's outline enters construction isolation and selects that original; source enters construction isolation and selects an original (while an opacity mask or a pattern is edited, it selects the original and the editing layer stays isolated); while a group's originals are isolated, it selects one of that group's originals → {id}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/shaper.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.arrowheads.edit",
   :label "Edit Arrowheads",
   :params
   "{} open the arrowheads file (a native document next to the preferences; created first with one example head when it is missing). Each symbol in it is one custom arrowhead named after the symbol: it points right, its registration point is the tip, and its height is drawn as wide as the built-in heads; its visible fills and outlined strokes make the head. Saving the file reloads the heads. Under automation read roots, a file outside them is an error, and nothing is made or opened → {path, created: whether the file was made now}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrowheads.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.arrowheads.reload",
   :label "Reload Arrowheads",
   :params
   "{} read the arrowheads file again (a save of it from VectorCraft does this already; under automation read roots, a file outside them is an error and is not read) → {count, skipped: [{name, reason}]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/arrowheads.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.set",
   :label "Stroke Options",
   :params
   "{weight?: pt, cap?: butt|round|square, join?: miter|round|bevel, miterLimit?, align?: center|inside|outside, dash?: [d,g,…]|null (a 0 dash with a round or projecting cap draws dots or squares; a new pattern keeps the current offset and alignment), dashOffset? (exact dashes only), alignDashes?: bool (true: dashes fitted to corners and path ends, every run between them holding whole periods with a dash centred on each corner and end; false, the default for a new pattern: exact lengths), startArrow?, endArrow?: Arrow|ArrowOpen|LineArrow|Barbed|Concave|DoubleArrow|HalfArrowLeft|HalfArrowRight|Chevron|Feather|Swallowtail|Triangle|TriangleOpen|TriangleReverse|TriangleBar|Kite|Leaf|Drop|Circle|CircleOpen|HalfCircle|Oval|Target|Square|SquareOpen|Tag|TagOpen|Diamond|DiamondOpen|Hexagon|HexagonOpen|Star|Cross|Plus|Bar|DoubleBar|DotOnBar|Slash|DoubleSlash|Bracket|Fork|null|{custom: name} (a custom arrowhead of the arrowheads file, stroke.arrowheads.list)|{Custom: {name, path}} (a custom head with its art, as document.inspect reports one; refused when the path fills no area, parts thinner than a millionth of a head unit counting as none, or has more than 4096 anchors, more than 4096 subpaths or a point more than 64 head units from the tip) (HalfArrowLeft/Right: one barb, left or right of the direction the head points), arrowAlign?: \"extend\" (tip past the end point, default)|\"tip\" (tip on the end point; the stroke is shortened), profile?: \"uniform\"|\"lens\"|\"taperStart\"|\"taperEnd\"|\"pinch\"|\"teardrop\"|\"wave\"|a saved profile's name (stroke.widthProfile.list), widthPoints?, gradientMode? (as document.inspect reports them in strokeOptions, so those read back unchanged; ignored here: a custom profile is set with the Width tool, gradientMode with paint.editGradient), item?: stroke item index|null (omitted: the Appearance panel's active item if it is a stroke, else the top stroke, created when missing), ids?|id?, target?: \"object\"|\"contents\", aligned?: bool (index and item are rows of the first target's stack: each other target edits its equal one, as the Appearance panel does for a mixed selection; with the art of a graph design in a series given first, rows of the art's stack: docs/mcp.md)} Without a stroke item, type takes weight, cap, join, miterLimit, align (around its glyph outlines; the type stays live) and the dash options as its characters' stroke (every run; text.setRangeStyle `strokeOptions` styles a range), and images and symbol instances (also in groups) are left alone. With nothing selected (and no ids) they set up the next object drawn (appearance.newArt; weight always does). On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores a weight it changes on the topmost visible stroke (docs/mcp.md); on a graph label's stroke row, the graph stores the label's topmost visible fill and stroke rows for every label of its kind, and on its characters the stroke options they take; on a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring, the graph stores the paint, weight, opacity and blend mode of its topmost visible fill and stroke rows that the edit changes, and the weight it writes to the topmost visible stroke, for every line of its kind, and not its caps, joins, dashes, alignment or arrowheads → {objects: how many objects took the stroke options}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stroke.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.setAdvanced",
   :label "Stroke Options",
   :params
   "{arrowScale?: [start %, end %], swapArrows?: bool, flipProfile?: \"along\"|\"across\", brush?: name|null, item?: stroke item index|null, aligned?: bool (as stroke.set), ids?|id?, target?: \"object\"|\"contents\"} Stroke panel extras (with nothing selected, all but brush set up the next object drawn)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stroke.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.weightDown",
   :label "Stroke Weight Down",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} lower each selected stroke's weight by one step, as stroke.weightUp raises it, down to a quarter unit (a thinner weight is kept) → {objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stroke.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.weightUp",
   :label "Stroke Weight Up",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} raise each selected stroke's weight by one step of Units › Stroke (a quarter unit below one unit, then whole units; up to 1000 pt), each from its own weight: the selected objects' active or top stroke, type's stroked characters; objects without a stroke are left alone. With nothing selected (and no ids), the weight of the next object drawn. On a path directly in a graph series, the graph also stores the new weight of the topmost visible stroke, and on a graph label the new weight of its characters' stroke or its stroke row for every label of its kind, and on a graph's axis line, tick mark or radar ring its rows for every line of its kind (docs/mcp.md) → {objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stroke.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.widthPoint.copy",
   :label "Copy Width Point",
   :params
   "{id, index: the width point to copy, t: 0..1 where the copy goes} → {index} (Alt-drag with the Width tool). Landing on another point makes a discontinuous point, as a stroke.widthPoint.set move does",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.widthPoint.remove",
   :label "Delete Width Point",
   :params
   "{id, index | indices: [..]} remove width points (removing the last one leaves a uniform stroke)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.widthPoint.set",
   :label "Width Point",
   :params
   "{id, t: 0..1 (fraction of the path length), left, right: side widths in pt, index?: width point to edit or move, adjustAdjoining?: bool (the nearest points either side change their widths in proportion, using the sampled widths for a new point)} → {index}. Without index a point already at t is replaced; a point moved onto another one's t joins it as a discontinuous point (on the side it came from), so the width steps there. Creates a uniform profile first if needed",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.widthProfile.add",
   :label "Add to Profiles",
   :params
   "{name?} save the selected stroke's variable width to the Profile list (kept with the preferences) under `name` (default \"Width Profile N\"; unique, not a built-in's) → {name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stroke.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.widthProfile.delete",
   :label "Delete Profile",
   :params
   "{name?} remove a saved profile from the Profile list (default: the selected stroke's); built-in profiles can't be deleted, and strokes keep their widths → {deleted}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stroke.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.widthProfile.reset",
   :label "Reset Profiles",
   :params
   "{} remove every saved profile, leaving the built-ins → {removed: count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/stroke.rs"}
  {:id "stroke.widthProfile.set",
   :label "Width Profile",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, points: [[t, left, right]…] (width factors, 1 = the stroke weight) | null = uniform}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/distortcmds.rs"}
  {:id "svgFilter.apply",
   :label "Apply SVG Filter",
   :params
   "{name, ids?|id?, item?, index?} apply the document's SVG filter `name`, or the default filter of that name when the document holds none (svgFilter.list), to ids or the selection as a live svg.filter effect, as one undo step, like effect.apply → {ids, index, item}; with index, the filter takes the place of the applied svg.filter effect at index of item, like effect.setParams → {ids}; a default is copied into the document in the same undo step, which is refused when the document already holds 64 filters",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/svgfilter.rs"}
  {:id "svgFilter.define",
   :label "New SVG Filter",
   :params
   "{xml: one SVG <filter> element (its id is its name; 1..64 primitives; at most 64 KB), replace?: the name of the filter it replaces and keeps (Edit SVG Filter)} add an SVG filter to the document, after the others, or replace one, as one undo step; every object whose svg.filter effect names it draws with the new definition; a name another filter of the document has is refused and a document holds at most 64 filters; replace with the name of a default filter the document does not hold adds the edited copy to the document under that name, and code equal to the default's adds nothing; a new filter may take a default's name, and then stands in its place → {name, filters}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/svgfilter.rs"}
  {:id "svgFilter.delete",
   :label "Delete SVG Filter",
   :params
   "{name} remove an SVG filter from the document, as one undo step; objects whose svg.filter effect names it keep the effect, which draws nothing until a filter of that name is defined or imported again, or the default of that name is applied; a default filter the document holds no copy of is refused (the defaults are not deleted), and deleting the document's copy of one lists the default again → {filters}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/svgfilter.rs"}
  {:id "svgFilter.import",
   :label "Import SVG Filter…",
   :params
   "{path?|svg?} add the <filter> elements of an SVG file (at most 16 MB; not SVGZ; its first 256 filters) or of SVG text to the document's SVG filters, as one undo step; a filter whose name the document already has, and one svgFilter.define would refuse, is left out; objects whose effect names an added filter draw with it → {added: [names…], skipped: count, filters}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/svgfilter.rs"}
  {:id "svgInteractivity.addFile",
   :label "Add JavaScript File",
   :params
   "{file: path or URL (written as given, without surrounding spaces)} link a JavaScript file to the document, after the others: SVG export writes a <script xlink:href> for each linked file. A file already linked (the same text) stays where it is; a document links at most 64 files → {files} (as svgInteractivity.info gives them)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/interactivity.rs"}
  {:id "svgInteractivity.clearEvents",
   :label "Clear Events",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?} remove every event from ids or the selection, as one undo step → {changed: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/interactivity.rs"}
  {:id "svgInteractivity.removeEvent",
   :label "Remove Selected Entry",
   :params
   "{event, ids?|id?} remove an event and its JavaScript from ids or the selection, as one undo step → {changed: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/interactivity.rs"}
  {:id "svgInteractivity.removeFile",
   :label "Remove JavaScript File",
   :params
   "{file} unlink a JavaScript file from the document: the file linked as `file` or, with automation read roots in force, a file outside them whose file name is `file`; an error, unlinking nothing, when `file` fits more than one → {files} (as svgInteractivity.info gives them)",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/interactivity.rs"}
  {:id "svgInteractivity.setEvent",
   :label "Add Event",
   :params
   "{event: \"onclick\"|\"onmouseover\"|… (svgInteractivity.info's eventNames), script: string (the JavaScript; \"\" removes the event), ids?|id?} set the JavaScript an event runs on ids or the selection, replacing the event's script where it has one, as one undo step; SVG export writes it as the event attribute → {changed: objects}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/interactivity.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.addUsedColors",
   :label "Add Used Colors",
   :params
   "{selection?: false (only the selected art's colours; default: all the art's), global?: false (the new swatches are global and the matching unlinked colours in that art link to them)} add a swatch for each colour used (fills, strokes, text, gradient stops, mesh points) that no solid swatch has yet, as one undo step → {added: [names], linked}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.delete",
   :label "Delete Swatch",
   :params
   "{name? | names?: [swatch or colour group names] (a group goes with its swatches), unlink?: true (art using a deleted global swatch keeps its colour, unlinked; false keeps the stale link)} delete in one undo step → {deleted, unlinked: paints unlinked}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.duplicate",
   :label "Duplicate Swatch",
   :params "{name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.edit",
   :label "Swatch Options",
   :params
   "{name, newName?, color? (e.g. {l, a, b} for a Lab colour; #rrggbbaa and #rgba are refused), keepModel?: bool (as paint.setFill; the swatch's own color and a color given with mode keep their model), mode?: \"gray\"|\"rgb\"|\"hsb\"|\"lab\"|\"cmyk\"|\"web\" (convert the colour), global?, spot? (spot colours are always global), paint?: paint.setFill params ({color}, {gradient} or {swatch}) or {pattern: name} replacing the swatch's colour; gradient or pattern with one of the same kind (stored as swatch.new stores it: a gradient keeps its aspect with or without start/end and holds no swatch link; a pattern is untransformed)} edit a swatch in any colour group, as one undo step. Fills, strokes, text, gradient stops and tint swatches linked to a global swatch take its new colour (at their own tint) and name; turning Global off unlinks them (they keep their colour). A fold line role the swatch carries (addon.packaging.roles) stays with it under its new name, and moves to a new swatch name when Global is turned off. Colour, mode and spot apply to solid colours only; a tint swatch only takes a new name (edit its base) → {name, relinked: paints changed}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.editGroup",
   :label "Edit Color Group",
   :params
   "{group: colour group, colors: [colour] (hex, key, {c,m,y,k} or {l,a,b}; #rrggbbaa and #rgba are refused; the group's swatches take them in order, extra colours become new swatches, swatches past the end are removed; built-in swatches can't change; a color the swatch already has keeps its model), keepModel?: bool (as paint.setFill), rename?: new group name} rewrite a colour group as one undo step; art linked to its global swatches takes their new colours (and keeps its colour, unlinked, when its swatch goes) → {name, swatches: [names], relinked}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.library.add",
   :label "Add to Swatches",
   :params
   "{library: id or name, names?: [swatch or colour group names in the library] (default: all of it; a group comes as a colour group, a single swatch ungrouped), apply?: \"fill\"|\"stroke\" (also apply the first one to the selection and the defaults, as paint.setFill / paint.setStroke), focus?: true (with apply: false keeps the active proxy)} copy library swatches into the document as one undo step. A swatch the document already has (same name and paint) isn't added again; a name taken by another swatch gets a number (\"Clay 1 2\"). A pattern swatch brings its pattern, as pasting art painted with it does: the same pattern the document has is used, and a name another pattern or swatch has gets a number → {library, added: [names in the document], existing: [names already there], applied?: name}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatchlib.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.library.copyToUser",
   :label "Copy to User Defined",
   :params
   "{library: id or name of a loaded library (category \"loaded\", swatch.library.load)} copy it into the user library folder of the desktop app, whose libraries VectorCraft lists as User Defined every time it starts (a loaded library is listed until the app quits): a library file as it is, the swatches of a document or a library loaded from data as a .vcswatches file. A name the folder already has gets a number (\"Brand 2.ase\") and no file is replaced; when the folder already holds the same file, that file is used. The library is then listed as User Defined only, and until the app quits commands given its loaded id use the copy; a User Defined library comes back as it is → {library: its User Defined id, name, count, path (left out when it is outside the read roots), copied: false when nothing was written}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatchlib.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.library.load",
   :label "Other Library…",
   :params
   "{path? | data?: file text | dataBase64?, name?: file name (default: the path's)} load a .vcswatches, .gpl, .ase (swatch exchange) or .acb (color book, read only) library, or the swatches of any document VectorCraft opens (see document.formats), for the library panel (Window → Swatch Libraries lists it until the app quits; a file of the user library folder, or a file with the same extension and bytes as one there, opens as that User Defined library) → {library: id, name, count}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatchlib.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.library.save",
   :label "Save Swatch Library…",
   :params
   "{path?, format?: \"vcswatches\" (lossless JSON: colour models, global, spot, gradients, groups) | \"gpl\" (8-bit RGB palette; groups as `# Group:` comments) | \"ase\" (swatch exchange, binary: solid colors in their own model (RGB, CMYK, Lab, Gray) as global, spot or process colors, and color groups; gradients are left out, and a tint swatch is saved as the color it shows) | \"css\" (custom properties on :root) (default: the path's extension, else vcswatches), names?: [swatch or colour group names] (default: all; None and patterns are never saved), name?: library name (default: the document's), user?: false (save into the user library folder, listed under User Defined)} save the document's swatches as a library → {path, format, count: the swatches written (gpl and ase hold solid colors only, and css leaves freeform gradients out), library?: id when saved to the user folder}; without path or user → {data: the file's text, format, count}, or {dataBase64, format, count} for ase",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatchlib.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.merge",
   :label "Merge Swatches",
   :params
   "{names: [two or more solid-colour swatches], name?: the merged swatch's name (one swatch kept)} keep the first (its name and colour) and delete the others; paints linked to them take its colour and link to it (or unlink when it isn't global), and gradient stops linked to them drop their process plates, as one undo step. When the kept swatch is global and carries no fold line role (addon.packaging.roles), it takes the role of the first merged swatch that carried one → {name, merged: [deleted names], relinked}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.move",
   :label "Move Swatch",
   :params
   "{name? | names?: [swatch names, in order; or colour group names to reorder the groups], to?: index in the destination (they go before the swatch or group now there; default: the end), group?: destination colour group (default: the ungrouped swatches; groups hold solid colours only)} reorder swatches or move them into or out of colour groups, as one undo step → {moved}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.new",
   :label "New Swatch",
   :params
   "{name?, color? | colors?: [colour | {swatch, tint?}] (one swatch each, in one undo step; #rrggbbaa and #rgba are refused; `{swatch, tint}` is the paint paint.setFill gives, so a tint of a global or spot color becomes a tint swatch) | swatch? | gradient? | pattern?: name (default: the current fill), tint?: 0..100 (% of the global or spot `swatch`, or of the one the current fill links to), mode?: \"gray\"|\"rgb\"|\"hsb\"|\"lab\"|\"cmyk\"|\"web\" (convert the colour; lab: CIE L*a*b*, how spot colours are usually defined), global?, spot? (a spot colour, always global), group?: colour group name (solid colours only; default: ungrouped), none?: true (the None paint), paint?: paint.setFill params, keepModel?: bool (as paint.setFill)} save a colour, gradient or pattern as a swatch. A tint of a global or spot colour (below 100%, without mode, global or spot) becomes a tint swatch, \"Name 40%\", linked to its base: it follows edits to the base and applies as that tint of it. A gradient swatch keeps the gradient's aspect (with or without start/end) and holds no link to the swatch its gradient came from, and a pattern swatch holds the pattern untransformed. Names are unique (\"Sky 2\"); a colour's default name is its values (\"C=10 M=20 Y=30 K=0\", \"R=255 G=128 B=0\", \"Gray K=40\", \"L=55 a=60 b=40\") → {name, names: [every new swatch]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.newGroup",
   :label "New Color Group",
   :params
   "{name?, swatches?: [names] (solid colours move into the group; gradients, patterns and None stay), colors?: [colour | {swatch, tint?}] (added as new swatches; #rrggbbaa and #rgba are refused; `{swatch, tint}` below 100% of a global or spot color adds a tint swatch, \"Name 40%\", linked to it, and any other `{swatch}` its color), keepModel?: bool (as paint.setFill), fromArtwork?: false (add the unique colours of the selected art: fills, strokes, text, gradient stops and mesh points; a colour linked to a global swatch moves that swatch into the group), toGlobal?: true (with fromArtwork: the new swatches are global and the selected art's matching unlinked colours link to them), includeTints?: false (with fromArtwork: tints of global swatches also get swatches of their own)} → {name, swatches: [names in the group], linked: paints linked}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatch.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.resetDefaults",
   :label "Default Swatches",
   :params
   "{replace?: false} bring back the default swatches and colour groups of the document's colour mode that are missing (by name), as one undo step; replace: true makes the swatches exactly the defaults (art linked to a removed global swatch keeps its colour, unlinked) → {added: [names]}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/swatchlib.rs"}
  {:id "swatch.setSpot",
   :label "Spot Color",
   :params
