  {:id "text.setStyle",
   :label "Character",
   :params
   "{ids?|id?, font?, style? (font alone: the style is kept when the new family has it, else its closest), size?: pt 0.1..1296 (outside it: an error), leading?: pt|\"auto\", tracking?: 1/1000 em, justify?: \"auto\" (the start of each paragraph's direction)|\"left\"|\"center\"|\"right\"|\"justifyAll\", fill?: colour|\"none\", stroke?: colour|\"none\" (characters without a stroke weight get 1 pt; #rrggbbaa and #rgba are refused in both), keepModel?: bool (fill and stroke, as paint.setFill), strokeWidth?: pt (the character stroke's weight, in document points as stroke.set), features?: [\"dlig\", \"-liga\", \"salt=2\", …] OpenType (swsh, ss01–ss20, salt, titl, pnum, lnum, sups, subs, numr, dnom and aalt take the font's alternate number as `tag=N`, N 0–65535: \"salt=2\" draws the second alternate of each glyph that has one, \"salt\" is \"salt=1\", \"-salt\" and \"salt=0\" are off; \"hkna\" is H or V Style, kana in the font's forms for the writing direction, shaped as `vkna` in vertical type, and \"ital\" is Roman Italics, half-width alphanumerics in the font's italic forms, both on or off only), featureChanges?: [\"tnum\", \"-onum\", \"salt=2\", …] (OpenType features turned on, or with - off, on top of each character's own, a value replacing the feature's last one; its other features are kept), start?: byte, end?: byte} (size/leading are document points after object scaling; with a range: the character attributes style that range and justify the paragraphs it touches; without: all the text; no undo step when no character, paragraph or graph label style changes) → {ids, overflow?: [id…] (area type and type on a path whose text no longer fits; left out when all fits), warning?: text (the font or style set isn't available: its type is drawn in the fallback font or the family's closest style)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/typecmd.rs"}
  {:id "text.setText",
   :label "Set Text",
   :params
   "{id?|ids?, text} replace the contents of text objects (keeps the first run's style); no undo step when no object changes (each already has the text in one style, every paragraph with the first one's attributes, and no ruby) → {ids, overflow?: [id…] (area type and type on a path whose text no longer fits; left out when all fits)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/typecmd.rs"}
  {:id "text.spelling.change",
   :label "Change All",
   :params
   "{to: string, words: [{id, start: byte, end: byte}…] (words of type objects, as text.spelling.check lists them; none overlapping)} replaces each word with to, all in one undo step, each object laid out once (Check Spelling's Change All); a word that already reads as to is left alone, and with no other word there is no edit and no undo step; an error, with nothing changed, when a word's bytes are not in its object's text → {changed: count of words replaced}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/spelling.rs"}
  {:id "text.startList",
   :label "Bullets and Numbering",
   :params
   "{id, at?: byte (default: the end of the text)} start a list from typed characters, what the Type tool runs when a space is typed on its own: when the text from the start of the paragraph that `at` is in up to `at` is \"1. \" or \"1) \" (a numbered list in 1, 2, 3), \"A. \" or \"A) \" (a numbered list in A, B, C), \"* \" (a bulleted list with the filled dot), \"+ \" (the hollow circle), \"# \" (the filled square) or \"> \" (the dash), and the paragraph is in no list, those characters are removed and the paragraph joins that list as one undo step (left and first-line indents of 0 become 18 and -18, as text.setFormat sets them); otherwise nothing changes → {id, started: bool, caret: byte (the paragraph's start when started, else `at`)}",
   :source "crates/engine/src/cmd/textedit.rs"}
  {:id "text.tabs.clear",
   :label "Clear All Tabs",
